{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C14 text: "Theorem 8.2 (The insight is not evidence). If the technology is truth-blind, conditioning on the production event adds nothing to the record: W equals the ordinary reflective posterior of m''s correctness given the record alone. Post-restoration fit is guaranteed by the restoration property, so passing the test carries no information beyond the record either. Among candidates in T that induce the same record distribution, prior odds are preserved exactly." \u8594? "Corollary 9.3 (Self-audit requires sufficiency for the candidates): The assessment (calT, nu) is expressible by agent i only if its current post-refinement partition P_i' is sufficient for every tau' in calT, hence only if P_i' refines the join of Proposition 7.5. This is necessary but not sufficient for complete computation of warrant. An agent holding a minimal restoration therefore generally cannot formulate the cross-representation comparison required to determine the sign or magnitude of its signed warrant gap; a broader-awareness assessor may be able to."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C14 condition: ['the technology is truth-blind', '(T, nu) is a reflective assessment problem: T is a finite set of candidate objective assignments and nu a full-support reflective prior'] \u8594? []\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C14 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#proof-thm-uninformative' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L964-L990'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C15 text: "Corollary 8.3 (Self-audit requires sufficiency for the candidates). The assessment (T, nu) is expressible by agent i only if P_i is sufficient for every tau' in T, hence only if P_i refines the join of Proposition 6.6. An agent holding a minimal restoration therefore generally cannot formulate the comparison that measures its own warrant gap: the overconfidence is invisible from within the representation that produces it. Short of that refinement, warrant must be supplied externally, by fresh evidence whose likelihoods differ across candidates, by an assessor with broader awareness, or by a future self." \u8594? "Example 1 (continued, Section 9): If firm i's technology produces the column refinement, the recoded record pins the unique consistent theory (architecture 0 on the first column, 1 on the second), and representation-relative coherence assigns it probability 1. With calT = \{row world, column world\} and a symmetric prior, the two worlds assign the realized diagonal-only record equal probability and the technology is truth-blind. So by Theorem 9.2, W(O_i) = 1/2 and the signed warrant gap is 1 - 1/2 = +1/2. The same gap applies to a firm that acquires the row refinement (coherence 1, warrant 1/2): confidence exceeds warrant even when the formulated theory is objectively correct. By Corollary 9.3 neither firm can conduct this assessment itself. One fresh differentiated observation at an off-diagonal state resolves the row/column identification problem completely; at beta = 1, any number of pooled observations remains nondiagnostic."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C15 condition: ['the assessment (T, nu) is expressible by agent i'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C15 main: True \u8594? False\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C15 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1069-L1116' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L941-L990'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C16 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 8). Suppose firm i's technology produces the column refinement. The recoded record pins the unique consistent theory (architecture 0 on the first column, 1 on the second) and representation-relative coherence assigns it probability one. In the reflective assessment with T = \{row world, column world\} and a symmetric prior, the two worlds generate identical records and the technology is truth-blind, so the reflective posterior equals the prior: W = 1/2, and the warrant gap is exactly one-half. The same gap afflicts the firm that acquires the row refinement: its coherence in the true assignment is also probability one and its warrant is also one-half. Neither firm can conduct this assessment itself, since expressing both candidate worlds requires the full partition into singletons. One fresh differentiated observation at an off-diagonal state closes the gap completely (the two worlds predict opposite labels there), while pooled observations, in any number, close nothing." \u8594? "Theorem 10.4 (Epistemic absorption): Under Assumption 10.3, almost surely: (a) at most n*(|S| - 1) refinements occur, and every agent's awareness partition is eventually constant; (b) only finitely many inquiry elections occur, because each agent stops electing once its achievability weight has decayed enough that lambda_i^(k){\i T}(max pi_i - min pi_i) < gamma_i, which happens after finitely many consecutive failures because B_hat_i is bounded and gamma_i > 0; (c) there is an almost surely finite period after which no agent's language changes and no agent pays an inquiry cost, and every agent's epistemic life thereafter is judged-Bayesian updating within a fixed language. Moreover, on the event that the standing profile is eventually constant: (d) every agent's active set is eventually constant; every retained theory is eta-adequate at every recurrent pair under terminal play; every theory eta-inadequate at a recurrent pair is eventually absent; and each agent is eventually either never dissonant or in dissonant stasis."\par}
