{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C18 evidence pointer: 'appendix/appendix.md:L86-L149' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#prop-adequacy'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C19 text: 'Proposition 9.8 (On-path adequacy, and where error lives). In a SCUE, every theory in the support of every mu_i is eta-adequate at every visited pair. All surviving falsity is confined to what the configuration does not expose: mechanism assignments at states pooled with causally different states whose mixture imitates a single mechanism at the visited profiles, and counterfactual claims at unvisited profiles.' \u8594? 'Proposition D.7 (Capacity: detection speed and robustness), as stated in the paper: in stochastic environments capacity is a single cognitive-style dial. Expected detection time under an exposed profile is O(b_i/D_i) (and Omega(b_i)), while spurious dissonance at a non-exposed rest point has probability at most exp(-b_i). A larger b_i lowers false-alarm risk but requires more accumulated evidence to detect a broken language, and capacity plays no role in the exact deterministic case.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C19 condition: ['the configuration is a SCUE (Definition 9.1)'] \u8594? ['marg_i theta(a)(x_i) > 0', 'D_i > 0', 'detection bound: an exposed standing profile whose evidence processes are freshly initialized when that profile begins', 'robustness bound: a non-exposed stochastic rest point entered under the hypotheses of Proposition D.5(ii-b)']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C19 main: True \u8594? False\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C19 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#proof-prop-adequacy' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#prop-capacity'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C2 text: 'Proposition 4.1 (No Bayesian emergence). Bayesian conditioning on any event measurable with respect to the algebra generated by P_i yields a posterior on Delta(M(P_i)). No sequence of such updates makes a theory outside M(P_i) expressible or a distinction finer than P_i usable in a policy.' \u8594? "Proposition 5.1 (No Bayesian emergence): Any well-defined judged or ordinary conditioning of a prior mu in Delta(M(P_i)) on an observation in the agent's observation algebra yields a posterior mu' in Delta(M(P_i)). No sequence of such updates makes a theory outside M(P_i) expressible or a distinction finer than P_i usable in a policy."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C2 condition: ['the event conditioned on is measurable with respect to the algebra generated by P_i'] \u8594? []\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C20 text: 'Proposition 9.9 (Persistent performance differences). There exist primitives and absorbing configurations in which agents hold different terminal partitions and theories, expected per-generation payoffs differ strictly and permanently, and no disadvantaged agent has a priced repair: for each such agent either B_i = 0 or lambda_i B_i < gamma_i. The proof is by the instances of Example 1.' \u8594? 'Proposition 10.5 (Persistent performance differences): There exist primitives and absorbing configurations in which agents hold different terminal partitions and theories, and expected per-period payoffs differ strictly and permanently, with no disadvantaged agent closing the gap. This is because, for each, the corrective process has died economically at one of its two stages: either its question is unpriced (dissonant stasis, lambda_i^(k_i)*B_hat_i(r_i) < gamma_i from some period on), or, having asked and refined, the policy change its new model recommends is priced below the switching hurdle (enlightened inertia, T-horizon gain <= kappa_i).'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C20 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1289-L1356' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1091-L1160'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C21 text: "Proposition 9.11 (No payoff-relevant error in diagnostic environments). In a diagnostic environment, every SCUE is free of payoff-relevant error. Payoff-relevant falsity survives only in environments that admit concealing profiles, and it requires them to be sustained: collective error needs the absence of both corrective forces, strategic variety inside agents' categories and environmental punishment of uniform misservice." \u8594? "Proposition D.9 (No payoff-relevant policy error in diagnostic environments), as stated in the paper: in environments whose primitives are diagnostic (payoff-relevant policy errors always expose the erring agent's awareness under confirmed stationary play), no SCUE contains a payoff-relevant policy error."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C21 condition: ['the primitives (Theta, tau, rho, u) are diagnostic (Definition 9.10)'] \u8594? []\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C21 main: True \u8594? False\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C21 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1306-L1410' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#prop-diagnostic'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C22 text: 'Example 1 (continued, section 9, the trap and its knife edge). Set beta = 1 and suppose both firms acquired the column refinement after the discovery generation and became certain of the false column assignment. Each then plays the column policy; the firms pool at every state; every payoff is one-half; and one-half is exactly what the column theory predicts under pooled play. The configuration is a SCUE with payoff-relevant error: policies are subjectively optimal, conjectures confirmed, no dissonance ever occurs (the profile is concealing), and B_i = 0 for both firms, so the configuration survives even a free, infallible inquiry technology; the warrant gap is permanent, each firm remaining exactly half-warranted as unbounded experience accumulates. Now let beta < 1: in the first generation containing an off-diagonal state, the pooled firms receive beta/2 where their theory predicts one-half; the demand side reveals the label, dissonance returns, leverage turns positive, and the reflective posterior becomes degenerate. Payoff-relevant self-confirmation is a knife-edge property of perfectly forgiving demand (the beta < 1 environments are diagnostic), and the destroyed value 1 - beta at each misserved episode is itself the corrective signal.' \u8594? 'Proposition D.10 (Strict punishment implies diagnosticity), as stated in the paper: strictly punishing primitives, whose on-path conditionals at every payoff-relevant policy error separate from every expressible prediction by more than eta, are diagnostic. Consequently every SCUE under strictly punishing primitives is free of payoff-relevant policy error.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C22 condition: None \u8594? ['min_\{m in M(P_i)\} TV(p_i*(.|C_\{P_i\}(s), a^sigma(s)), marg_i m(C_\{P_i\}(s))(a^sigma(s))) > eta']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C22 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1306-L1356' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#prop-punishing'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C23 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 9, persistence). With beta = 1, let firm 1 hold the row refinement and the true assignment while firm 2 remains coarse with gamma_2 > lambda_2 B_2. Firm 1 wins both off-diagonal states and splits the rest, earning three-quarters to firm 2's one-quarter, forever; firm 2 sits in dissonant stasis, its question priced below its cost. Every route out (strategic variety, demand harshness, cheaper inquiry) is exactly one of the model's named forces." \u8594? 'Example 1 (continued, Section 10). The trap: at beta = 1, if both firms acquired the column refinement and became certain of the false column assignment, they pool at every state and every payoff is 1/2, exactly what the column theory predicts. The configuration is a SCUE with payoff-relevant error, and the positive signed warrant gap is permanent: each firm remains exactly half-warranted. The knife edge: for beta < 1, the first period serving an off-diagonal state pays beta/2 where the theory predicts 1/2, so dissonance returns, B_hat turns positive and the reflective posterior becomes degenerate; payoff-relevant self-confirmation is a knife-edge property of perfectly forgiving demand. Persistence: at beta < 1, firm 1 holds the row refinement and the true assignment while firm 2 stays coarse and is dissonant from t_0. If gamma_2 > lambda_2^(k_\{2,t_0\})*B_hat_2(r_\{2,t\}) for every subsequent record (for which gamma_2 > lambda_2^(k_\{2,t_0\}){\i T}(max pi_2 - min pi_2) suffices), firm 2 never elects and is in dissonant stasis. Its balanced four-token record with T = 2 gives L_2^fine = 1, L_2^cur = 0, J_2 = 1 and B_hat_2 = 1/2, and under uniform rho the firms earn 3/4 and 1/4 per period, permanently. At beta = 1 the continuation is either a one-switch path into renewed dissonance or a stable policy-inertia path, not an indefinite oscillation.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C23 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1289-L1356' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md:L190-L236'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C24 text: 'Bayesian learning operates only within the current language, and a misspecified posterior grows confident rather than alarmed, so detecting representational failure requires a distinct faculty: causal dissonance, the statistical rejection of every expressible theory. Bayesian updating cannot expand the language and cannot even detect that expansion is needed; detection is statistical dissonance, a faculty distinct from the posterior.' \u8594? 'Confidence can grow even as every expressible theory fails: updating does not sound an alarm when the space itself is broken, because posterior mass always sums to one, so a manager whose every expressible theory is false can grow steadily more confident in the least false among them.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C24 condition: None \u8594? ['every expressible theory is false']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C24 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L503-L533' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#rem-self-sealing'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C25 text: "When every represented theory is false, the posterior does not sound an alarm: by the logic of misspecified Bayesian learning (Berk 1966), it concentrates on the least wrong of the available theories, and the agent grows more confident, not less; within-language updating is self-sealing. In the stochastic setting (Remark 4.2), when every expressible theory is false because the agent's cell mixes mechanisms, a full-support posterior does not signal this: it concentrates on the expressible theories closest to the on-path conditionals in Kullback\u8211?Leibler divergence, and the agent becomes increasingly {\i confident} in a wrong theory. Posterior mass always sums to one; the inadequacy of the whole model class is not an event in the agent's algebra, so detecting that the language itself is broken requires a faculty outside the posterior\u8212?the consistency test." \u8594? 'Experience directs repair without determining it (without selecting its answer), so insight, economical representation change, is necessarily fallible: the requirement that a successful repair reconcile the retained record directs inquiry without determining its output.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C25 condition: ["every represented (expressible) theory is false: the agent's cell mixes mechanisms, so no cell-constant assignment matches the on-path conditionals", 'the posterior has full support'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C25 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#rem-self-sealing' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#nonidentification-and-the-price-of-robustness'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C26 text: "Dissonance directs inquiry without determining its output. The record restricts admissible repairs\u8212?every restorative refinement must separate the evidence clusters that no single mechanism can accommodate\u8212?but generally many minimal repairs remain, observationally equivalent worlds demand different answers, and no truth-blind technology can be uniformly correct. Fallibility is the price of a representation that economizes on distinctions: any inquiry process meeting the paper's disciplines must be fallible." \u8594? "Discovering that one's causal language has failed, and repairing it, are different cognitive operations from ranking the answers the language allows, and only the ranking is Bayesian: ranking the answers one can express and judging whether any expressible answer is adequate are different cognitive operations, and only the first is Bayesian."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C26 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L710-L838' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L370-L388'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C27 text: 'Questions die rationally: sustained success extinguishes them, and defeat concentrates both the evidence and the incentive to inquire in the losing firm. Rational cessation: an agent whose record contains no evidence against its current actions has $B_i=0$, so sustained success extinguishes inquiry even though awareness remains incomplete.' \u8594? 'Leverage prices action separation, not uncertainty reduction, and the difference shows in who inquires: after a later stretch of play, the firm holding the true theory faces no unresolved action margin and values its question at zero, while its defeated rival values the same question at one half. Success, not ignorance, is what extinguishes the demand for new theories.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C27 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L915-L1011' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#example-1-continued-4'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C28 text: 'The return to Bayes is disciplined by a warrant account: because any successful repair fits the experience that generated it by construction, retrospective fit carries no information, and\u8212?when inquiry is truth-blind\u8212?neither does the arrival of the insight itself. Post-insight confidence therefore exceeds warrant by a computable gap, and an agent holding a minimal repair generally cannot even formulate the comparison that would measure its own gap: the agent returns to the Bayesian world carrying a warrant gap of known location and generally unknowable (to it) size.' \u8594? 'Validation must come from new evidence that discriminates: it requires evidence whose likelihood differs across relevant candidate worlds, and fresh evidence changes reflective warrant only when its likelihood differs across the represented candidate worlds; otherwise further awareness expansion may be required before the agent can use the evidence for that comparison. Because the agent may lack the awareness needed to formulate that comparison, this gives boards, investors, and other broader-awareness outsiders a precise epistemic role that retrospective coherence cannot play.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C28 condition: ['for the arrival of the insight to carry no information: inquiry is truth-blind'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C28 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#sec-pivot' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L964-L990'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C29 text: "Because theories cause actions and actions generate the evidence, almost surely awareness change and inquiry die out, leaving every agent permanently inhabiting a Bayesian world\u8212?models fit, questions are dead, inquiry is priced below cost. The configurations in which the process rests, self-confirming unawareness equilibria, can preserve false theories, heterogeneous awareness (heterogeneous causal languages), and permanent performance differences, and they do so precisely when neither of the two corrective forces\u8212?strategic variety inside an agent's categories, or an environment harsh enough to punish misservice observably\u8212?is present: heterogeneous causal languages, and the performance differences they support, persist exactly when these strategic and environmental conditions fail to erase them." \u8594? 'Inquiry is an economic process, and it can die in every way an economic process dies: the question is answered, it is priced below its cost, it is abandoned after repeated failure, or it was never answerable.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C29 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1192-L1356' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1016-L1030'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C3 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 4). Under the coarse partition P_i^0 = \{S\}, firm i's expressible theories are the constant assignments m^0, m^1, m^n. The row law tau is inexpressible: no reweighting of \{m^0, m^1, m^n\}, on any evidence, produces it. A firm that later observes payoffs irreconcilable with all three theories finds its posterior undefined, not alarmed: misspecification announces itself only because likelihoods hit zero exactly; with stochastic mechanisms no announcement would occur at all." \u8594? "Example 1 (continued, Section 5): Under the coarse partition, firm i's expressible theories are the constant assignments m^0, m^1, m^n. The row law tau(s_rc) = theta^r is inexpressible: no reweighting of \{m^0, m^1, m^n\}, on any evidence, produces it. After successive deterministic observations eliminate the expressible theories one by one, the observation that eliminates the last theory with positive posterior mass produces a zero Bayesian normalizer, so ordinary conditioning itself is undefined. With stochastic full-support mechanisms the Bayesian normalizer remains positive and no such announcement occurs."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C3 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L469-L543' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L370-L394'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C30 text: 'Strategic variety is traced to its source: agents with identical preferences, identical data-processing (Bayesian) competence, and identical objective opportunities, facing the same objective system, end up with different causal languages, different theories, and different payoffs because their experiences posed different questions, their technologies produced different repairs, and their subsequent positions extinguished further inquiry at different points. Terminal heterogeneity in awareness is path dependence in the strong sense, and this is a microfoundation for heterogeneity that begins before probability does: why similar firms perform differently receives an answer that begins before beliefs\u8212?because they came to different questions, and some questions died before they were asked.' \u8594? 'Identical firms facing identical environments can end with different languages, different theories, and permanently different payoffs, for reasons that precede any prior.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C30 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1289-L1356' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1091-L1104'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C31 text: 'Bryan et al. (2022) bring unawareness into value capture and show that awareness itself earns rents; the present paper models where the awareness advantage originates, which that paper leaves open.' \u8594? 'Where unawareness has been linked to value capture (Bryan et al. 2022), the present model explains a possible origin of the awareness advantage.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C31 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#unawareness-and-growing-awareness' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1091-L1104'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C32 text: 'Under unawareness the grain-of-truth condition can fail at the level of language: the truth may be inexpressible. This paper supplies the missing dynamics: statistical dissonance is the detector of language-level failure; awareness refinement restores the grain of truth on the path of play\u8212?after each successful refinement, some expressible theory matches the visited conditionals within tolerance; and the fixed-language models are recovered exactly as the special case in which awareness never changes.' \u8594? 'The terminal analysis adds two epistemic possibilities to the fixed-hypothesis-space models: self-confirming unawareness equilibrium requires a surviving represented class and no worthwhile question, while dissonant stasis permits rational cessation outside a Bayesian world; enlightened inertia adds a policy condition: even after an improved policy becomes representable, its finite-horizon gain may not clear the switching hurdle. Together these conditions show how restoration of a viable represented class, termination of inquiry, and continuation of play can diverge.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C32 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1129-L1172' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1016-L1030'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C33 text: 'On-path data constrain $F$ only at visited state\u8211?profile pairs, so observationally equivalent systems with different counterfactual content are generic; that is the engine of the identification results.' \u8594? 'Every dissonant record is repairable under the exact calibration but not in general. With deterministic mechanisms every dissonant record is repairable, and finiteness of $\\\\Pi(S)$ ensures a minimally restorative refinement exists; existence is guaranteed only in the deterministic case. With stochastic mechanisms, multiple observations at a single state may yield empirical conditionals for which no one mechanism satisfies equation (6) across the observed profiles; because no refinement can split a state, such a record has $\\\\mathcal R(\\\\mathcal P_i,\\\\bar r_i)=\\\\emptysetset$ and is irreparable: dissonance names a defect that no expressible refinement can repair.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C33 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L783-L838' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-irreparable'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C34 text: 'Restricting theories to single mechanism assignments, rather than arbitrary conditional distributions per cell, is substantive: if any distribution were expressible, any within-cell mixture would be too, and no experience could reject the class; coarseness alone cannot produce a detectable failure in a saturated model space.' \u8594? "If no agent's awareness ever changes, the model is a repeated interaction among subjectively rational Bayesian learners in the sense of Kalai and Lehrer (1993) and Ryall (2003), and its stable configurations are self-confirming equilibria (Fudenberg and Levine 1993)."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C34 condition: None \u8594? ["no agent's awareness ever changes"]\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C34 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L345-L450' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L999-L1014'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C35 text: "Rivals with finer partitions condition on distinctions agent $i$ cannot see, so the within-cell state mixture of an on-path conditional can vary with the profile; it is precisely this dependence\u8212?differentiated play by others inside one's own categories\u8212?that generates the contrasts on which the diagnostic apparatus feeds." \u8594? 'Under exact deterministic testing, dissonance implies that the current partition is insufficient for the objective assignment: an expressible true deterministic theory could not be rejected.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C35 condition: None \u8594? ['exact deterministic testing (the exact calibration)']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C35 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#on-path-conditionals' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md:L41-L44'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C36 text: "Within fixed awareness, learning is ordinary: if no agent's awareness ever changes, the model is a repeated interaction among subjectively rational Bayesian learners in the sense of Kalai and Lehrer (1993) and Ryall (2003), and its stable configurations are self-confirming equilibria (Fudenberg and Levine 1993)." \u8594? "Two recurring mechanisms generate exposure: heterogeneity inside a cell surfaces either because other agents play differently across the pooled states (strategic differentiation inside one's categories, which changes the visited profiles and the induced mixtures) or because the environment punishes uniform play across causally different states in an observable way."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C36 condition: ["no agent's awareness ever changes"] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C36 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#def-scue' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1108-L1160'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C37 text: 'Because restriction always applies to the unrestricted tier, the acting belief is well defined whenever the active set is nonempty\u8212?including when a fluctuating test empties the set and later refills it\u8212?provided the reference posterior gives the refilled set positive mass.' \u8594? 'Token sets are mutually incoherent when no single mechanism accommodates their union, and every restorative refinement must separate mutually incoherent sets. In the deterministic running example incoherence is a binary relation between labeled periods and restoration is a graph-coloring problem; in general, a mixture of three mechanisms may defeat every single mechanism even though each pair of tokens is individually accommodatable, so restoration is a hypergraph coloring.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C37 condition: ['the active set is nonempty', 'the reference posterior gives the refilled set positive mass'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C37 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#judged-updating' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md:L272-L350'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C38 text: 'In the deterministic case no assumption is needed for judged updating, since rejection coincides with a zero-likelihood event, refill cannot occur, and judged updating reduces to ordinary Bayesian conditioning.' \u8594? 'Minimal restorations, when they exist, are typically multiple, as the running example shows vividly.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C38 condition: ['mechanisms are deterministic'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C38 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L591-L617' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#example-1-continued-3'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C39 text: "Exposure has two sources: heterogeneity inside a cell surfaces either because other agents play differently across the pooled states\u8212?strategic differentiation inside one's categories, which changes the visited profiles and the induced mixtures\u8212?or because the environment punishes uniform play across causally different states in an observable way. Both reappear as the corrective forces of the population dynamics." \u8594? "Irreparability is an analyst-level property: it is a fact about $\\\\bar r_i$, and the agent, lacking the state labels, cannot in general tell an irreparable record from a repairable one; this is precisely the agent's inability to distinguish causal heterogeneity from mechanism noise."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C39 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#prop-exposure' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md:L309-L347'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C4 text: "Lemma 5.2 (Test consistency). Fix a committed profile played in all generations and suppose no theory's distance to an on-path conditional equals eta exactly. As generations accumulate, almost surely every eta-adequate theory is eventually always in the active set and every eta-inadequate theory is eventually never in it." \u8594? 'Lemma D.1 (Test consistency), as stated in the paper: sequential testing is consistent. A theory strictly inadequate at a recurrent pair is almost surely rejected, an adequate theory is falsely rejected with conditional probability at most E_i^m(t_0)*exp(-b_i), and the active set is monotone and eventually constant.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C4 condition: ['a committed profile is played in all generations', 'TV(p_i*(. | C, a), marg_i m(C)(a)) != eta for every theory m and visited pair (C, a)'] \u8594? ['TV(p_i*(.|C,a), marg_i m(C)(a)) != eta']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C4 main: True \u8594? False\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C4 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#proof-lem-test-consistency' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C40 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 5). Belief heterogeneity, by inducing differentiated play, is what made the shared language's failure visible: heterogeneous priors commit the firms to differentiated constant policies, differentiated play at $s_\{00\}$ and $s_\{11\}$ empties both active sets, and pooled play would have concealed the failure." \u8594? 'At an irreparable record, if the deliberative record still admits a positive-leverage coherent grouping, the agent may elect a doomed inquiry until its achievability weight decays; if no coherent grouping prices the question, it declines immediately.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C40 condition: None \u8594? ['the record is irreparable']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C40 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L663-L683' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-irreparable'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C41 text: 'Token sets are mutually incoherent when no single mechanism accommodates their union; every restorative refinement must separate mutually incoherent sets, since a cell containing both would be incoherent.' \u8594? 'Under recurring visitation irreparability is typically transient, but a record whose critical pairs stop being visited can remain irreparable forever, a possibility classified within dissonant stasis.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C41 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L710-L722' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-irreparable'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C42 text: 'Minimal restorations, when they exist, are typically multiple\u8212?as the example shows\u8212?and existence itself is guaranteed only in the deterministic case.' \u8594? 'Rational cessation: an agent for whose record no coherent grouping yields positive representational increment has $\\\\widehat B_i=0$, so sustained success can extinguish inquiry even though awareness stays incomplete; and, by the decay of $\\\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$, so can sustained failure: a true, valuable, repairable question can be rationally abandoned.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C42 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L724-L755' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#prop-participation'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C43 text: 'Remark 6.3 (Irreparable records). With deterministic mechanisms, restoration is always possible: the singleton partition recodes each token to its own state, where the generating mechanism fits exactly. With stochastic mechanisms this guarantee fails: an unlucky finite sample at a single state can produce an empirical conditional outside the tolerance of every mechanism, and no partition of $S$ can separate observations generated at the same state; then $\\\\mathcal R(\\\\mathcal P_i,r_i)=\\\\emptysetset$ and the record is irreparable. Because $\\\\mathcal R$ is computable from the record, the agent recognizes irreparability; the technology fails surely; and the participation rule assigns the question no value, so no inquiry cost is wasted on it. Under recurring visitation irreparability is transient, but a record whose critical pairs stop being visited can remain irreparable forever.' \u8594? 'Away from pointwise transparency, enlightened inertia can be unanticipated because pre-insight leverage is only an estimate and the realized refinement may deliver a different gain. Under pointwise transparency, by contrast, exact and repair-invariant leverage can make later enlightened inertia foreseeable; the model nevertheless preserves the two-stage timing as a deliberate simplification.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C43 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L736-L779' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#rem-stickiness'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C44 text: 'The participation rule is a coherent non-Bayesian criterion operating precisely where Bayes is undefined, and its variables respect every discipline of section 3.5: the leverage quantifies over retained tokens and their recorded outcomes, never over candidate representations.' \u8594? 'Determinism certifies that two tokens sharing an observed pair but differing in consequence are distinct states, and under the stronger record-level condition of pointwise transparency the deliberative leverage estimate becomes exact and repair-invariant.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C44 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L840-L948' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-certification'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C45 text: 'The valuation horizon of equation (6) is one full anticipated recurrence of the retained record, so $B_i$ grows as evidence accumulates; any fixed-horizon normalization\u8212?per episode, per generation\u8212?rescales $B_i$ and $\\\\gamma_i$ together and changes nothing.' \u8594? "In the running example at the discovery record, under the model's two-stage timing a firm may still elect inquiry when the participation condition holds; in this transparent case, a hurdle at or above the exact gain makes later enlightened inertia foreseeable, a consequence of the deliberate timing convention rather than of unawareness."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C45 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L889-L982' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L842-L862'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C46 text: "The inner minimum over $\\\\Theta_i(t)$ in equation (6) is where counterfactual transparency lives. When consequences identify forgone values\u8212?as in winner-take-all markets, where a lost episode's record pins the mechanism every repair must assign it\u8212?the minimum is over a singleton and the bound is exact; the laboratory's leverage of one-half is this case. When consequences conceal forgone values, $\\\\Theta_i(t)$ is large, the minimum drags each term toward zero, and $B_i$ understates the objective value of repair: opaque environments rationally suppress inquiry." \u8594? 'In the running example the discovery-record valuation used no conjecture about the rival and no reference to which refinement might arrive; transparency (winner-take-all) makes each $\\\\Theta_i(g)$ a singleton, so the deliberative estimate is exact.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C46 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L866-L982' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L852-L870'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C47 text: 'Nothing in Bayesian coherence determines the bridge prior $\\\\mu_i^\{+\}$ from the pre-dissonance belief\u8212?the domains differ\u8212?and this nonuniqueness is not a defect to be repaired but the boundary between insight and judgment.' \u8594? "In the running example, in a later stretch that serves the two off-diagonal states, by which point firm 1 has acquired the row refinement (certain of the true assignment) while firm 2 has acquired the column refinement (certain of the false one), their policies differ at those states, firm 1 wins both, and the labels revealed there falsify firm 2's column theory."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C47 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1013-L1026' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#example-1-continued-4'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C48 text: 'Truth blindness is the polar case: were production correlated with the objective assignment\u8212?social transmission from an informed source\u8212?the arrival of the insight would itself be evidence, and the adjustment could move confidence in either direction.' \u8594? "In the running example's later stretch, the losing firm 2, holding the column refinement, upon success reaches complete awareness in one step: both column cells must split."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C48 condition: ['production is correlated with the objective assignment (e.g., social transmission from an informed source)'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C48 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#thm-uninformative' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#example-1-continued-4'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C49 text: 'Example 1 (continued, section 8). The warrant gap of one-half also afflicts the firm that acquires the row refinement: its coherence in the true assignment is also probability one, and its warrant is also one-half. Unwarranted certainty is not a symptom of error\u8212?early confidence outruns the evidence even when it happens to be right, and what separates the two firms is the objective law, which neither observes.' \u8594? 'Nothing in Bayesian coherence determines the bridge prior $\\\\mu_i^\{+\}$ from the pre-dissonance belief (the domains differ), and this nonuniqueness is not a defect to be repaired but the boundary between insight and judgment.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C49 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1038-L1116' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L872-L891'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C5 text: 'Proposition 5.5 (Exposure and dissonance). Under a fixed committed profile, agent i experiences dissonance from some generation onward almost surely if and only if P_i is exposed.' \u8594? 'Proposition 6.5 (Exposure and dissonance): Fix a standing profile and suppose no theory sits exactly at the adequacy boundary. If every theory that is eta-adequate under the fixed profile remains active when that profile begins at t_0, then P_i is exposed if and only if eventual dissonance occurs almost surely. If the profile is not exposed and m is an active eta-adequate theory at entry, then, conditional on the entry history, dissonance is avoided forever with probability at least 1 - E_i^m(t_0)*exp(-b_i). If some such m satisfies E_i^m(t_0) <= 1, this bound is at least 1 - exp(-b_i).'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C5 condition: ['a fixed committed profile', 'TV(p_i*(. | C, a), marg_i m(C)(a)) != eta for every theory m and visited pair (C, a) (the hypothesis of Lemma 5.2, through which the proof runs)'] \u8594? ['TV(p_i*(.|C,a), marg_i m(C)(a)) != eta', 'E_i^m(t_0) <= 1']\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C5 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L571-L653' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L461-L476'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C50 text: 'Example 1 (continued, section 8). One fresh differentiated observation at an off-diagonal state closes the warrant gap completely\u8212?the two worlds predict opposite labels there\u8212?while pooled observations, in any number, close nothing: warrant, like leverage, is purchased with differentiated action.' \u8594? 'An agent or outside observer who does not possess the complete analyst record may genuinely learn from a truth-blind output because it conveys information about the hidden particulars on which production operated.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C50 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1038-L1116' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#thm-uninformative'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C51 text: "A SCUE in which every partition is sufficient for $\\\\tau$ and beliefs concentrate near the truth is simply a self-confirming equilibrium; the concept's interest lies entirely in the other cases." \u8594? 'Truth blindness is the polar case; if production, formulation, or bridge-prior selection remains correlated with the objective assignment after conditioning on the record and history (as with transmission from an informed source), the output can supply a genuine Bayes factor, and the adjustment can move warrant in either direction.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C51 condition: ['every partition is sufficient for tau', 'beliefs concentrate near the truth'] \u8594? None\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C51 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#def-scue' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#thm-uninformative'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C52 text: 'Part (d) of Theorem 9.4 and the rest-point characterization are conditional on play stabilizing, which in every configuration featured in this paper is immediate: their beliefs make one action per cell strictly dominant. If the success bound of Assumption 9.3(ii) is dropped, one further absorbing pattern becomes possible: perpetually elected, perpetually failing inquiry\u8212?a question worth asking that is never answered.' \u8594? 'In the running example, one fresh differentiated observation at an off-diagonal state resolves the row/column identification problem completely because the two worlds predict opposite labels there: if the formulated theory is correct, $W(O_i)$ rises to one and the positive signed gap closes; if it is false, it is rejected, the singleton active set empties, and the acting belief becomes undefined.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C52 evidence pointer: 'appendix/appendix.md:L28-L165' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L941-L990'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C53 text: 'Remark 9.7 (Rational anomaly tolerance). Zero-leverage dissonant stasis is a recognizable condition, not a pathology of the model: the agent knows its causal account is broken\u8212?every expressible theory is rejected\u8212?yet the break disturbs no represented action comparison, so repairing it is worth nothing; anomaly tolerance is rational precisely when pinned distinctions carry no robust action leverage. At an irreparable record, $\\\\mathcal R=\\\\emptysetset$, no expressible repair exists at any price, and the anomaly is not merely unprofitable to fix but impossible to fix within the current grammar.' \u8594? 'Successful refinement restores a nonempty represented model class consistent with the retained record. It does not by itself establish objective correctness or future on-path adequacy; subsequent experience determines whether the restored language survives.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C53 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L915-L948' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L563-L650'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C54 text: 'Strategic variety has a pre-probabilistic source: agents with identical preferences, identical Bayesian competence, and identical objective opportunities diverge because their experiences posed different questions, their technologies produced different repairs, and their positions extinguished inquiry at different points. Heterogeneous prior understanding generates heterogeneous questions; questions generate heterogeneous languages; languages generate heterogeneous theories, plans, and payoffs. This sequence begins before probability does, and it is path-dependent in the strong sense: the order of experiences shapes the terminal language, and agents can converge to the same behavior while retaining permanently different representations.' \u8594? 'Switching costs temper the cycling of standing policies within a Bayesian world: the inaction band absorbs belief fluctuations too small to be worth acting on, so only swings whose horizon-$T$ gain exceeds $\\\\kappa_i$ move play, a stabilizing force, though not one that rules out large-amplitude cycles.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C54 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1289-L1356' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#rem-scope'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C55 text: "The value of experimentation is not information: a question is worth asking when some admissible answer would change action, not when its resolution would be most informative. High-entropy uncertainty with no action leverage is rationally ignored, and narrow contrasts that straddle an action threshold are rationally pursued. This explains rational cessation\u8212?why successful firms stop asking\u8212?and the loser's advantage in inquiry: competitive defeat concentrates the evidence, the dissonance, and the incentive in the defeated firm." \u8594? 'Abandoned questions are a substantive absorbing outcome, not an artifact: inquiry ceases because it is answered, because it is unpriced, or because it is given up.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C55 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L915-L1011' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1016-L1030'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C56 text: "Early confidence outruns evidence even when correct. A founder's theory that beautifully organizes the experiences that generated it has, by Theorem 8.2, earned nothing by that organization: the fit was guaranteed by construction. Validation requires evidence whose likelihood differs across the candidate worlds, and, by Corollary 8.3, the founder typically cannot even express the comparison, which is a formal argument for outside challenge (boards, investors, advisors with different awareness) as a warrant technology rather than a monitoring technology." \u8594? "Were $\\\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$ held fixed instead of decaying, an agent could elect a doomed inquiry forever, paying $\\\\gamma_i$ each period for a repair that never arrives; the decay rules this out and is the model's account of when a rational inquirer stops."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C56 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1038-L1116' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#rem-scope'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C57 text: "Markets discipline theories through two channels: payoff-relevant collective error requires both concealment by play and forgiveness by demand. Industries where customers absorb misservice\u8212?captive buyers, no substitutes, third parties bearing the cost\u8212?can sustain shared false theories indefinitely; industries with strong outside options discipline theories even under consensus. Where demand is forgiving, the only corrective is strategic variety in beliefs, which gives belief heterogeneity a social value distinct from its private value: the entrant with a deviant theory is the industry's epistemic infrastructure." \u8594? "Zero-leverage dissonant stasis is a recognizable condition: the agent registers that no admitted theory survives its test, yet its deliberative valuation finds no coherent grouping with positive representational increment, so repairing the account is worth nothing to it; anomaly tolerance is rational precisely when the agent's coherent groupings carry no gross representational leverage."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C57 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1306-L1410' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#prop-participation'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C58 text: 'Anomaly tolerance is an equilibrium phenomenon: firms that know their causal account is broken and rationally decline to fix it are not failing at learning; their standing anomalies carry no action leverage. The model predicts where tolerated anomalies accumulate: in transparent-consequence environments, near decisions whose robust optimum is insensitive to the unresolved structure.' \u8594? 'At an irreparable record no expressible repair exists at any price (the anomaly is not merely unprofitable but impossible to fix within the current grammar), though the agent, unable to certify irreparability under noise, may keep electing while its deliberative record supports positive leverage and until the achievability weight decays.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C58 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1192-L1275' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-irreparable'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C59 text: 'Performance differences persist in this model not because an equilibrium concept freezes them but because the process that would erase them has died economically: the disadvantaged configuration generates no dissonance, or generates no leverage, or prices its question below the cost of asking.' \u8594? 'Terminal heterogeneity in awareness is path dependence in the strong sense: agents with identical preferences and identical Bayesian competence, facing the same objective system, end at different languages and different payoffs because their histories posed different questions.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C59 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1289-L1356' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1091-L1104'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C6 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 5, opening policies). With beta = 1 and heterogeneous priors over the constant theories (firm 1 considers theta^0 more likely than theta^1, firm 2 the reverse), a direct computation shows that, against any conjecture about the rival, offering architecture 0 is subjectively strictly dominant for firm 1 and architecture 1 for firm 2 whenever mu_i(m^a) > (2 - beta) mu_i(m^a'); at beta = 1 this is simple belief asymmetry. The firms therefore commit to differentiated constant policies." \u8594? "Example 1 (continued, Section 6): Let beta = 1, with heterogeneous priors (firm 1 considers theta^0 more likely than theta^1, firm 2 the reverse). Against any conjecture, offering architecture 0 is subjectively strictly dominant for firm 1, and architecture 1 for firm 2, whenever mu_i(m^a) > (2 - beta)*mu_i(m^a'); at beta = 1 this is simple belief asymmetry, so the firms adopt differentiated constant policies. With T = 2 and two periods serving s_00 and s_11 under differentiated play, firm 1 wins at s_00 (payoffs 1, 0) and loses at s_11 (payoffs 0, 1). No constant assignment is consistent with both observations (m^0 fails at s_11, m^1 at s_00, and m^n predicts 1/2 at both), so each firm's active set empties: causal dissonance in its exact deterministic form. Had the firms pooled on the same architecture at both states, each would have received 1/2 every period, consistent with all three constant theories; the pooled profile is concealing. Belief heterogeneity, by inducing differentiated play, is what made the shared language's failure visible."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C6 evidence pointer: 'appendix/appendix.md#dominance-thresholds' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L461-L493'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C60 text: "The paper's absorbing configurations extend self-confirming equilibrium with two epistemic conditions\u8212?the language survives its own evidence, and no question is worth its price\u8212?and it is these conditions, not the strategic ones, that carry the new results." \u8594? 'Agents identical in preferences, competence, capacity, and cost can still end at different languages and payoffs, because their histories posed different questions and their truth-blind technologies produced different repairs: path dependence that begins before probability.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C60 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1129-L1172' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1091-L1104'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C61 text: 'The distinction matters for how the theory-based view should treat \u8220?updating\u8221?: ranking the answers one can express and judging whether any expressible answer is adequate are different cognitive operations, and only the first is Bayesian.' \u8594? 'Agents identical in everything but their dissonance capacity $b_i$ and switching hurdle $\\\\kappa_i$ also diverge: in stochastic environments capacity affects detection speed and the robustness of rest points, while the hurdle sets the propensity to enlightened inertia; the capacity channel disappears under exact deterministic contradiction.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C61 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L503-L533' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1089-L1104'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C62 text: 'In the deterministic running example incoherence is a binary relation between labeled episodes and restoration is a graph-coloring problem; in general, a mixture of three mechanisms may defeat every single mechanism even though each pair of tokens is individually accommodatable, so restoration is a hypergraph coloring.' \u8594? 'Of the two origins of terminal heterogeneity, the first (different question histories and repairs) is the awareness-path microfoundation and the second (differences in dissonance capacity and switching hurdle) a parametric cognitive-style one, and neither is available in the fixed-language tradition.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C62 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#prop-coherence' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1099-L1107'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C63 text: 'How much an environment lets agents price their own questions is itself a dimension of its diagnosticity, alongside exposure.' \u8594? 'Concealment is necessary, not sufficient: an objectively false theory that retains nonvanishing acting-belief mass in a stable SCUE must be $\\\\eta$-adequate on path, so the induced profile is concealing for that theory; shared false theories can remain viable when play pools states that a coarse language treats alike, but concealment alone does not guarantee survival.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C63 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#rem-transparency' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1108-L1125'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C64 text: 'A SCUE is a configuration in which the grain of truth holds on-path for every agent and no one has a priced reason to look for the off-path remainder.' \u8594? 'Strict payoff and separation margins at a fixed profile survive small perturbations of the primitives, though this is a local stability property rather than openness of global diagnosticity.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C64 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L1129-L1172' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#rem-local-robustness'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C65 text: "The model supplies the theory-based view with the object its formal treatments presuppose and, in doing so, changes what several of the view's claims mean." \u8594? "In the persistence configuration of the running example, for realized record compositions other than the balanced four-token record, the coarse firm's gross representational leverage remains positive when some coherent grouping supplies a positive increment and is bounded as in Proposition 8.4."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C65 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#implications-for-the-theory-based-view' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#prop-participation'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C66 text: 'The model draws a formal boundary between learning within a causal language and producing a new one, and it prices the crossing.' \u8594? 'The running example illustrates several routes out of the trap and of dissonant stasis: strategic variety, demand harshness, and cheaper or more hopeful inquiry.'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C66 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L114-L131' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md:L1121-L1166'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C7 text: "Example 1 (continued, section 5, discovery and concealment). In a generation in which s00 and s11 are served under differentiated actions, the winner-take-all payoffs reveal the objectively preferred architecture at each state: firm 1 wins at s00 (payoffs 1, 0) and loses at s11 (payoffs 0, 1). No constant assignment is consistent with both episodes (m^0 fails at s11, m^1 at s00, and m^n predicts one-half at both), so each firm's active set empties: causal dissonance in its exact deterministic form. Had the firms instead pooled on the same architecture at both states, each would have received one-half at every episode, consistent with all three constant theories: the pooled profile is concealing, and coarse awareness would have survived its own evidence indefinitely." \u8594? "Proposition D.2 (Cellwise coherence), as stated in the paper: restoration factorizes cell by cell, so finding a repair is a coloring problem. For a candidate refinement P', M_hat_i^R(P', r_bar_i) = product over C' in P' of Theta_i^R(C'|r_bar_i), and P' is restorative if and only if every cell of P' is repair-coherent (Theta_i^R(C'|r_bar_i) nonempty)."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C7 condition: None \u8594? []\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C7 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md:L663-L683' \u8594? 'appendix/appendix.md#prop-coherence'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C8 text: "Proposition 6.2 (Cellwise coherence). Call a cell of a refinement coherent if some single mechanism passes the test on the cell's recoded observations. Then Mhat_i(P', r_i) != emptyset if and only if every cell of P' is coherent." \u8594? "Theorem 7.4 (Observational nonidentification): Fix common initial epistemic states, common record-measurable behavioral and tie-breaking rules, common truth-blind inquiry-and-formulation rules, and a finite horizon of H periods. Let tau != tau' be objective assignments whose joint consequence laws agree, tau(s)(a) = tau'(s)(a), at every state-profile pair reachable through H under either world. The two worlds admit a coupling under which, through H, their state draws, full consequence profiles, analyst and deliberative records, partition paths, beliefs, conjectures, standing policies, and production-and-formulation outputs coincide pathwise; if the equality holds at every pair reachable at any finite horizon, the coupling extends to the entire process. Consequently, no truth-blind inquiry-and-formulation rule can produce an objectively correct formulation with probability one in both worlds. More generally, the same conclusion holds for any success criterion whose sets of realizable outputs are disjoint across the two worlds."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C8 condition: ["P' strictly refines P_i and the retained record is recoded to the cells of P'"] \u8594? ["tau != tau'"]\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C8 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#proof-prop-coherence' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#proof-thm-nonidentification'\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C9 text: "Theorem 6.5 (Observational nonidentification). Let tau != tau' be objective assignments inducing the same distribution over agent i's records under the committed profiles played. Then any truth-blind technology, and any truth-blind inquiry-and-formulation rule, has the same output distribution in both worlds. If no single theory is eta-adequate under both worlds at the visited pairs, no truth-blind rule selects an adequate formulation with probability one in both." \u8594? "Proposition 7.5 (Robust sufficiency): A partition sufficient for every assignment in a candidate set calT must refine join_\{tau' in calT\} P^tau', the coarsest partition that refines every candidate causal-equivalence partition. A representation guaranteed to accommodate all observationally equivalent worlds is accordingly finer than any single world requires; a technology that economizes on distinctions must accept fallibility."\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C9 condition: ["tau != tau'", "tau and tau' induce the same distribution over agent i's records under the committed profiles played", 'the technology and the inquiry-and-formulation rule are truth-blind', 'for the second statement: no single theory is eta-adequate under both worlds at the visited pairs'] \u8594? []\par}
{\pard\li360\fi-360\sa60 \'95\tab C9 evidence pointer: 'paper/paper.md#proof-thm-nonidentification' \u8594? 'paper/paper.md#nonidentification-and-the-price-of-robustness'\par}
