{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -  text: 'Existing models show how theories guide learning, how Bayesian agents discriminate among represented\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    causal structures, and how play can reveal previously unavailable actions. This paper models a different\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    transition: an agent''s causal language pools objectively different situations; strategic experience\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    endogenously reveals an action-relevant failure of that pooling and thereby creates a localized open\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    question; costly inquiry activates a fallible technology whose output is not measurable in the agent''s\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    prior awareness; only after that output is formulated does the agent construct a prior and undertake\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    Bayesian judgment, under an explicit account of how much confidence the generating experience licenses.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    Because actions depend on theories, play can either create the contrasts that generate questions or\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    suppress them, so the model also delivers the population-level answer: when theory heterogeneity and\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    performance differences persist, and when the market erases them.'\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +  text: 'Existing work explains learning and action once theories, vocabularies, or awareness advantages\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    exist; this paper supplies the pre-Bayesian passage from represented-class failure to a question,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    a fallible new representation, formulation, and renewed Bayesian judgment. Its distinctive economic\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    and epistemic results are that an agent can value a finer actionable distinction before representing\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    its answers, and that evidence generating a truth-blind representation cannot be counted again as\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    independent validation. Embedding that passage in strategic interaction provides a mechanism by which\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    play exposes or conceals coarse languages and establishes the existence of absorbing configurations\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    with heterogeneous terminal languages and payoffs. The contribution is therefore upstream: question\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    histories and rational stopping points can generate strategic heterogeneity before priors over the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    resulting theories are available. The paper endogenizes the strategically consequential transition\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    into a new hypothesis space while leaving the semantic act that produces it primitive.'\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +  question: 'How an actor whose causal language has failed comes to possess a new one: the step before a\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    theory, or at least a hypothesis space, exists.'\par}
