{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -empirical conjectures converging to the constant induced play.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The event $E=\\\{$standing profile eventually constant$\\\}$ is future-dependent, so we handle the conditioning by coupling rather than by conditioning on $E$ directly.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Decompose $E=\\bigcup_\{G_2,\\sigma^\{*\}\}E_\{G_2,\\sigma^\{*\}\}$ over the countable set of (period, deterministic profile) pairs, where $E_\{G_2,\\sigma^\{*\}\}$ is the event that the standing profile equals $\\sigma^\{*\}$ from period $G_2$ on and $G_2>G^\{*\}$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Fix $(G_2,\\sigma^\{*\})$ and an agent $i$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Define an *auxiliary* process that plays $\\sigma^\{*\}$ in every period from $G_2$ on, driven by the same i.i.d. draws $(s_t,U_t)$; its post-$G_2$ draws are independent of $\\mathcal F_\{G_2\}$, so almost-sure statements about it hold conditional on the (arbitrary) $\\mathcal F_\{G_2\}$-measurable prefix and carry no conditioning bias.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +On $E_\{G_2,\\sigma^\{*\}\}$ the actual and auxiliary observations coincide from $G_2$ on, so any almost-sure property of the auxiliary process holds almost surely on $E_\{G_2,\\sigma^\{*\}\}$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For the auxiliary process, let $a_\{\\sigma^\{*\}\}(s)$ be the action profile induced by $\\sigma^\{*\}$ at state $s$, and define $S_\{\\sigma^\{*\}\}(C,a)=\\\{s\\in C:a_\{\\sigma^\{*\}\}(s)=a\\\}$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Call a pair $(C,a)$ *recurrent* if $S_\{\\sigma^\{*\}\}(C,a)\\neq\\emptysetset$ and *frozen* otherwise.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A frozen pair is visited only in the finite pre-$G_2$ prefix, so its count and constraint are constant.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A recurrent pair is visited each period with fixed probability $\\rho(S_\{\\sigma^\{*\}\}(C,a))>0$ independently, so its count diverges and, by the strong law on the finite space $X_i$, its cumulative empirical conditional converges to $p_i^\{*\}(\\cdot\\mid C,a)$; the finite prefix contributes a vanishing fraction.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +By [assumption 10.3](../paper/paper.md#ass-regularity)(i), [lemma D.1](#lem-test-consistency) applies to the auxiliary process: every theory active at $G_2$ and strictly inadequate under $\\sigma^\{*\}$ at a recurrent pair is eventually rejected, every theory inactive at $G_2$ remains absent, and the active set eventually becomes a survivor subset $A_i^\{*\}$ whose retained members are $\\eta$-adequate under $\\sigma^\{*\}$ at every recurrent pair.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Recurrently adequate theories may nevertheless be absent from $A_i^\{*\}$ because they were excluded when the current language was initialized, were rejected before $G_2$, or are stochastically false-rejected afterward.\par}
