{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -## B. Supporting computations for the running example \{#app-example\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Proof of Proposition [D.5](#prop-rest-points)(i) \{#proof-of-proposition-i\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Suppose awareness and standing policies are eventually constant almost surely, conjectures and reference posteriors converge, and each non-stasis agent's standing policy is a strict no-switch point at the limit (strict slack below $\\kappa_i$, or the strict $U_i$-argmax when $\\kappa_i=0$), with the stasis agents' carried-forward policies fixed.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Condition (i) of [definition 10.1](../paper/paper.md#def-scue) holds at the limit: by continuity of the finite-dimensional payoff comparison in $(\\mu_i,q_i)$, the strict slack persists near the limit\u8212?or, when $\\kappa_i=0$, the strict argmax keeps $\\sigma_i^\{\\star\}=\\sigma_i$ so the gain stays zero\u8212?and no switch is triggered, so the eventually constant standing policy is stationary under the switching rule.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For condition (ii), empirical conjectures converge to the frequencies induced by the eventually constant profile, giving limit agreement.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For condition (iii), a non-stasis agent is eventually never dissonant by [theorem 10.4](../paper/paper.md#thm-absorption)(d), and judged updating keeps the acting belief supported on the eventual active set $A_i^\{*\}$, whose members are $\\eta$-adequate at every recurrent pair, so the mass on any $\\eta$-inadequate theory is eventually zero.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For condition (iv), elections cease by [theorem 10.4](../paper/paper.md#thm-absorption)(b).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The limiting configuration thus satisfies the SCUE conditions for every non-stasis agent with the stasis agents' play held fixed\u8212?a partial SCUE.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 + \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Proof of Proposition [D.5](#prop-rest-points)(ii-a) \{#proof-of-proposition-ii-a\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +With deterministic mechanisms, rejection is irreversible.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Because the entry configuration satisfies [definition 10.1](../paper/paper.md#def-scue)(iii), its active set contains at least one $0$-adequate theory: otherwise every currently active theory would eventually be rejected and, since refill is impossible, the active set would remain empty thereafter.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A $0$-adequate theory matches every on-path observation and is therefore never rejected.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The active set consequently remains nonempty, although it may shrink as initially active inadequate theories are rejected.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Dissonance never occurs; $\\widehat B_i=0$ at every generated record by hypothesis, so no election or refinement occurs; and strict optimality under every conjecture and every theory in the entry active set fixes $\\sigma_i$ as that set shrinks and as reference posteriors and empirical conjectures evolve.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Empirical conjectures converge to induced play, and any initially active inadequate theory is eventually rejected.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The SCUE conditions therefore continue to hold.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 + \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Proof of Proposition [D.5](#prop-rest-points)(ii-b) \{#proof-of-proposition-ii-b\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Condition on the entry history $\\mathcal F_\{t_0\}$ and couple the actual process to the auxiliary process that holds the configuration's standing profile fixed after $t_0$; on the persistence event below the two coincide.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Fix an agent $i$ and an entry-active theory $m$: by hypothesis it is $\\eta$-adequate under the fixed profile and has $E_i^\{m\}\\le1$ at entry.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Adequacy makes $(E_i^\{m\})_\{t\\ge t_0\}$ a nonnegative supermartingale, so Ville's inequality gives\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\Pr\\!\\left(\\sup_\{t\\ge t_0\}E_i^\{m\}\\ge e^\{b_i\}\\,\\middle|\\,\\mathcal F_\{t_0\}\\right)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\le E_i^\{m\}(t_0)\\,e^\{-b_i\}\\le e^\{-b_i\},\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +so $m$ is never rejected off an event of probability at most $e^\{-b_i\}$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Agent $i$ becomes dissonant only if *every* entry-active theory is rejected\u8212?an event contained in \u8220?$m$ is rejected\u8221? for any single $m$\u8212?so that too has probability at most $e^\{-b_i\}$; a union bound over agents leaves probability at least $1-\\sum_i e^\{-b_i\}$ that no agent is ever dissonant.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +On that event each active set stays nonempty and, by permanence of rejection, remains contained in the entry set and hence supported on $\\eta$-adequate theories.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The strict-optimality hypothesis then fixes each standing action under every conjecture and every acting belief judged updating can produce, so $\\sigma_i^\{\\star\}=\\sigma_i$ and no switch fires; a nonempty active set makes $\\widehat B_i=0$, so no election fires.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Play therefore never changes, empirical conjectures converge to the induced play, and the SCUE conditions hold in every period.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In the deterministic case $\\eta=0$ every false-alarm probability is zero and the conclusion holds surely.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 + \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
