{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At an awareness cell $C$, write $p^a=\\mu_i(\\\{m:m(C)=\\theta^a\\\})$ for $a\\in\\\{0,1\\\}$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Against a rival playing $0$, the subjective expected-payoff difference between own actions $0$ and $1$ is $\\tfrac12p^0-(1-\\tfrac\{\\beta\}\{2\})p^1$; against a rival playing $1$ it is $(1-\\tfrac\{\\beta\}\{2\})p^0-\\tfrac12p^1$; mixtures follow by linearity.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Action $0$ is strictly dominant on $C$ if and only if $p^0>(2-\\beta)p^1$, and symmetrically.\par}
