{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -unawareness (Karni and Vier\\o 2017), intertemporal settings (Vier\\o 2021),\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -unforeseen evidence (Piermont 2021), and learning under incomplete\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -awareness (Grant et al. 2022).  Schipper (2021)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -distinguishes learning, which discards conceived possibilities, from\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -discovery, which adds unconceived ones, and shows how play can move players\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -to richer games; Schipper (2025) shows that beliefs about novelty can be\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -held without representing the novel objects\u8212?a precedent for the delabeled\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -constructs used here.  Relative to this literature the paper endogenizes what\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -those models take as given: the expansion event itself.  Experience generates\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the defect, the defect localizes the question, a fallible technology produces\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the new distinction, and the bridge prior problem\u8212?which reverse Bayesianism\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -constrains but does not solve\u8212?is embedded in an explicit account of what\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the generating evidence can and cannot warrant.  In strategy,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Bryan et al. (2022) bring unawareness into value capture and show\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -that awareness itself earns rents; the present paper models where the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -awareness advantage originates, which that paper leaves open.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Standard state spaces cannot represent nontrivial unawareness (Dekel et al. 1998), whereas generalized structures represent multiple awareness levels and interactive beliefs (Heifetz et al. 2006; Heifetz et al. 2013).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Reverse Bayesianism constrains belief revision under expansion (Karni and Vier\\o 2013), with extensions to awareness of unawareness, intertemporal choice, unforeseen evidence, and incomplete-awareness learning (Karni and Vier\\o 2017; Vier\\o 2021; Piermont 2021; Grant et al. 2022).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Discovery adds unconceived possibilities rather than discarding conceived ones (Schipper 2021), and beliefs about novelty need not represent the novel objects (Schipper 2025).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +This paper supplies an endogenous trigger, economic demand, and record-dependent constraints for awareness expansion while retaining semantic production as a primitive operation.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +It connects the defect that generates a question to a fallible refinement and then to bridge-prior formation and warrant.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Where unawareness has been linked to value capture (Bryan et al. 2022), the present model explains a possible origin of the awareness advantage.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The contribution is thus neither an endogenous derivation of semantic creativity nor another rule for updating on an enlarged space.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +It identifies when the old space fails, what the retained record requires of a repair, why the agent may pay for an unnamed distinction, and what the generating evidence warrants after that distinction arrives.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  ### Causal learning with a fixed vocabulary \{#causal-learning-with-a-fixed-vocabulary\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Causal graphical models separate intervention from association\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -(Pearl 2009; Spirtes et al. 2000); Ryall (2009) brings this machinery to\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -strategy, modeling imitation as Bayesian inference over operating structures\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -in which passive observation narrows candidates to an\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -observational-equivalence class and experimentation may discriminate among\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -survivors.  Active-learning methods select interventions to split a\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -represented equivalence class (He and Geng 2008).  These models are the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -benchmark for the paper's second learning tier: inference over structures\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -expressible in a fixed vocabulary.  The paper begins where they stop\u8212?when\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -no expressible structure is adequate\u8212?and its nonidentification results\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -extend the equivalence-class logic to the choice among vocabulary repairs:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -observationally equivalent worlds can demand different distinctions, so no\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -truth-blind repair rule is uniformly correct.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Causal graphical models distinguish intervention from association (Pearl 2009; Spirtes et al. 2000); in strategy, Bayesian inference over represented operating structures narrows candidates to an observational-equivalence class that experimentation may split (Ryall 2009), and active learning selects interventions within such a class (He and Geng 2008).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +These methods begin after the causal vocabulary is fixed.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +This paper studies failure and repair of that vocabulary: when no expressible structure remains adequate, experience constrains but need not identify the new distinction, and observationally equivalent worlds can require different repairs.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Once refinement and formulation create a new represented class, conventional interventions and Bayesian discrimination can again operate among its members.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  ### Subjective rationality and self-confirming equilibrium \{#subjective-rationality-and-self-confirming-equilibrium\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -The back end follows Kalai and Lehrer (1993) and Fudenberg and Levine (1993):\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -beliefs correct on the path of play need not be correct off it, and\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -subjectively optimal behavior against such beliefs can persist.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Ryall (2003) showed that competitive advantage can rest entirely on\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -rivals' self-confirming false theories.  Those models fix the hypothesis\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -space; convergence results in the rational-learning tradition require a grain\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -of truth\u8212?the truth absolutely continuous with respect to beliefs\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -(Kalai and Lehrer 1993).  Under unawareness the grain-of-truth condition can\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -fail at the level of language: the truth may be inexpressible.  This paper\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -supplies the missing dynamics.  Statistical dissonance is the detector of\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -language-level failure, awareness refinement restores the grain of truth on\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the path of play, and the fixed-language models are recovered exactly as the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -special case in which awareness never changes.  The paper's absorbing\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -configurations extend self-confirming equilibrium with two epistemic\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -conditions\u8212?the language survives its own evidence, and no question is worth\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -its price\u8212?and it is these conditions, not the strategic ones, that carry\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the new results.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Subjective rationality permits on-path-correct beliefs and subjectively optimal behavior to persist despite off-path error (Kalai and Lehrer 1993; Fudenberg and Levine 1993), and competitive advantage can rest on rivals' self-confirming false theories (Ryall 2003).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +These models fix the hypothesis space, while rational-learning convergence requires a grain of truth in represented beliefs (Kalai and Lehrer 1993).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +When truth is inexpressible, this paper supplies a process for diagnosing failure and restoring a viable represented class.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Its terminal analysis adds two epistemic possibilities: self-confirming unawareness equilibrium requires a surviving represented class and no worthwhile question, while dissonant stasis permits rational cessation outside a Bayesian world.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Enlightened inertia adds a policy condition rather than a third theory of learning: even after an improved policy becomes representable, its finite-horizon gain may not clear the switching hurdle.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Together these conditions show how restoration of a viable represented class, termination of inquiry, and continuation of play can diverge.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  ### Statement of contribution \{#statement-of-contribution\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Existing models show how theories guide learning, how Bayesian agents\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -discriminate among represented causal structures, and how play can reveal\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -previously unavailable actions.  This paper models a different transition.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -An agent's causal language pools objectively different situations;\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -strategic experience endogenously reveals an action-relevant failure of that\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -pooling and thereby creates a localized open question; costly inquiry\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -activates a fallible technology whose output is not measurable in the agent's\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -prior awareness; only after that output is formulated does the agent\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -construct a prior and undertake Bayesian judgment, under an explicit account\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -of how much confidence the generating experience licenses.  Because actions\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -depend on theories, play can either create the contrasts that generate\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -questions or suppress them\u8212?so the model also delivers the population-level\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -answer: when theory heterogeneity and performance differences persist, and\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -when the market erases them.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
