{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -product architectures $A_i=\\\{0,1\\\}$.  The mechanism vocabulary is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\Theta=\\\{\\theta^0,\\theta^1,\\theta^n\\\}$, with a demand parameter\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\beta\\in[0,1]$: under $\\theta^a$ (\u8220?architecture $a$ is preferred\u8221?), if the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -firms differentiate, the firm offering $a$ receives payoff $1$ and its rival\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$0$; if they pool on $a$, each receives $\\tfrac12$; if they pool on the other\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -architecture, each receives $\\beta/2$, the customer withholding $1-\\beta$ of\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the unit value.  Under $\\theta^n$ (\u8220?architecture is neutral\u8221?), each firm\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -receives $\\tfrac12$ regardless.  A consequence $x_i$ is the pair (own payoff,\par}
