{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The *deliberative leverage* is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\widehat B_i(r_i)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\begin\{cases\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\displaystyle\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\frac\{T\}\{\\lvert r_i\\rvert\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\max\\!\\left(\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\\{0\\\}\\cup\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\\{J_i(G;r_i):G\\in\\mathcal G_i(r_i)\\\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\right),\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +&\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\widehat M_i(\\mathcal P_i,r_i)=\\emptysetset,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\\\[1.1em]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +0,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +&\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\widehat M_i(\\mathcal P_i,r_i)\\neq\\emptysetset.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\end\{cases\} \\tag\{7\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The premise is that the empirical token *distribution* recurs, so the horizon-$T$ estimate is $T$ times the average per-token gross representational increment.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The outside option $0$ represents declining to attribute actionable value to any available grouping; it also makes leverage zero when $\\mathcal G_i(r_i)=\\emptysetset$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The current-language term is a counterfactual valuation benchmark, not a new dissonant policy-switching rule: at dissonance the standing policy continues to be carried forward under [assumption 4.4](#ass-commitment) unless inquiry succeeds.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Thus $\\widehat B_i$ prices the incremental gross action value of making a coherent grouping actionable beyond what one action per current awareness cell can already obtain, not a complete net expected-payoff value after switching costs.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Proposition 8.4 (Participation) \{#prop-participation\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$\\widehat B_i(r_i)$ is well defined, nonnegative, bounded by $T(\\max \\pi_i-\\min \\pi_i)$, and computable from the deliberative record, the standing policy, and the agent-known model primitives and test calibration.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At a dissonant record, electing inquiry has represented value $\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i(r_i)-\\gamma_i$, so agent $i$ elects if and only if\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i(r_i)\\geq\\gamma_i.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Moreover, at a dissonant record, $\\widehat B_i(r_i)>0$ if and only if some coherent grouping has positive representational increment:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +J_i(G;r_i)>0\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\qquad\\text\{for some \}G\\in\\mathcal G_i(r_i).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Thus a question is priced positively only when some coherent reading of the record supports action variation within at least one current awareness cell that robustly outperforms the best action kept uniform on that cell under the same coherent reading.\par}
