{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The record is finite, so it has finitely many groupings.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For every coherent group, $\\Theta_i(g)$ is a nonempty finite set, and all action and consequence spaces are finite.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Hence every max\u8211?min expression and every $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}(G;r_i)$, $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}(G;r_i)$, and $J_i(G;r_i)$ is well defined.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The set whose maximum appears in equation (7) always contains $0$, including when $\\mathcal G_i(r_i)=\\emptysetset$, proving existence and nonnegativity.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For fixed $C$ and $G$, put $f_\{C,g\}(a_i)=\\sum_\{t\\in r_i(C,g)\}\\Delta_i^G(t,a_i)$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Then\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\sum_\{g\\in G\}\\max_\{a_i\}f_\{C,g\}(a_i)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\geq\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\max_\{a_i\}\\sum_\{g\\in G\}f_\{C,g\}(a_i),\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +because the left side permits a separate maximizing action for every intersection while the right side restricts them to a common action.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Summing across current cells gives $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}(G;r_i)\\geq L_i^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}(G;r_i)$ and hence $J_i(G;r_i)\\geq0$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Writing $\\Delta \\pi_i=\\max \\pi_i-\\min \\pi_i$, each $\\Delta_i^G(t,a_i)\\leq\\Delta \\pi_i$, so $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}(G;r_i)\\leq\\lvert r_i\\rvert\\Delta \\pi_i$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For each current cell $C$, selecting its standing action $a_i=\\sigma_i(C)$ gives zero gain for every token in that cell, so $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}(G;r_i)\\geq0$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Therefore $0\\leq J_i(G;r_i)\\leq\\lvert r_i\\rvert\\Delta \\pi_i$, which gives $\\widehat B_i(r_i)\\leq T\\Delta \\pi_i$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Computability follows by finite enumeration using only the deliberative record, the standing policy, and the agent-known model primitives and test calibration.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The election rule is the achievability-weighted represented gain net of the inquiry cost.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Finally, because every $J_i(G;r_i)$ is nonnegative and the outside option is zero, the maximum in equation (7) is strictly positive exactly when some coherent grouping has strictly positive representational increment. \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The participation rule is a coherent non-Bayesian criterion operating precisely where the acting belief is undefined, and it respects every discipline of [section 4.6](#sec-commitments): $\\widehat B_i$ quantifies over the agent's own remembered tokens and the groupings it can articulate\u8212?\u8220?situations like the ones I lost will recur, and a distinction that sorted them would let me act on them\u8221?\u8212?never over named future representations.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For each coherent reading, the current-language benchmark first values the best action already expressible uniformly on each current awareness cell; gross representational leverage is only the additional robust gain from conditioning action on the finer grouping.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The estimate can be wrong, and honestly so: the agent does not know whether a distinction realizing its best grouping exists, which is why $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$ prices achievability.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Two comparative properties organize the applications.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +*Action separation, not information*: the value of a question tracks whether a finer distinction could improve action beyond the best current-cell-uniform response, not how much residual uncertainty remains; an agent for whom no coherent grouping yields positive representational increment declines to inquire.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +*Rational cessation*: an agent for whose record no coherent grouping yields positive representational increment has $\\widehat B_i=0$, so sustained success can extinguish inquiry even though awareness stays incomplete; and, by the decay of $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$, so can sustained failure\u8212?a true, valuable, repairable question can be rationally abandoned.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Enlightened inertia \{#rem-stickiness\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The model deliberately treats acquiring a distinction and acting on it as sequential decisions.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Pre-insight the agent uses $\\widehat B_i$ as a gross estimate of representational leverage, while the known switching hurdle $\\kappa_i$ is applied only after a concrete refinement, belief, conjecture, and policy make the realized horizon gain well defined ([assumption 4.4](#ass-commitment) and [proposition 8.4](#prop-participation)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +This timing is a bounded-rationality modeling convention, not a logical implication of unawareness.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Once inquiry delivers a concrete refinement, the realized gain may fail to clear $\\kappa_i$, so the agent carries its old policy forward despite knowing that its earlier causal account was incomplete.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Away from pointwise transparency, that enlightened inertia can be unanticipated because pre-insight leverage is only an estimate and the realized refinement may deliver a different gain.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Under pointwise transparency, by contrast, exact and repair-invariant leverage can make later enlightened inertia foreseeable; the model nevertheless preserves the two-stage timing as a deliberate simplification.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Enlightened inertia remains a second source of persistence, distinct from an unpriced question, whether or not mechanisms are deterministic, and it feeds the performance differences of [section 10](#sec-dynamics).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Determinism certifies that two tokens sharing an observed pair but differing in consequence are distinct states, and under the stronger record-level condition of pointwise transparency the deliberative leverage estimate becomes exact and repair-invariant; the full statement is [remark D.4](../appendix/appendix.md#rem-certification) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
