{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -### Definition 8.1 (Reflective assessment, warrant, and the gap) \{#def-warrant\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -A reflective assessment problem is a pair $(\\mathcal T,\\nu)$: a finite set\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -of candidate objective assignments and a full-support reflective prior.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Given the record and a successful production-and-formulation event, the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -*selection-adjusted warrant* $W$ of $(\\mathcal P_i',m')$ is the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\nu$-posterior probability that $m'$ is objectively correct\u8212?that\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\tau'(s)=m'(C_\{\\mathcal P_i'\}(s))$ for all $s$\u8212?conditional on the record\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -*and* on the production event.  The *warrant gap* $G$ is the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -representation-relative coherence probability of $m'$ minus $W$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -### Theorem 8.2 (The insight is not evidence) \{#thm-uninformative\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -If the technology is truth-blind, conditioning on the production event adds\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -nothing to the record: $W$ equals the ordinary reflective posterior of\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$m'$'s correctness given the record alone.  Post-restoration fit is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -guaranteed by the restoration property, so passing the test carries no\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -information beyond the record either.  Among candidates in $\\mathcal T$ that\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -induce the same record distribution, prior odds are preserved exactly.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At the discovery record ($T=2$, diagonal states served), each firm holds two tokens sharing the profile $(0,1)$ but differing in payoff: firm 1 won at $s_\{00\}$ and lost at $s_\{11\}$, firm 2 the reverse.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Because mechanisms are deterministic, the conflicting payoffs *certify* the two tokens as distinct states ([remark D.4](../appendix/appendix.md#rem-certification)), and the agent's best coherent grouping splits them: on the winning token the fine optimal gain is zero, while on the losing token switching to the pinned architecture gains $\\tfrac12$ against every rival action\u8212?a differentiated loss becomes a pooled half, or a pooled half a differentiated win.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Thus $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}=\\tfrac12$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Under the coarse one-cell current language, keeping the standing action gives aggregate gain zero, while switching uniformly gains $\\tfrac12$ on the losing token and loses $\\tfrac12$ on the winning token, so $L_i^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}=0$ and $J_i=\\tfrac12$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Consequently $\\widehat B_i=(2/2)(\\tfrac12)=\\tfrac12$ for both firms\u8212?identical gross representational leverage from opposite experiences\u8212?so each elects iff $\\lambda_i^\{(0)\}\\widehat B_i\\geq\\gamma_i$, i.e. $\\lambda_i^\{(0)\}/2\\geq\\gamma_i$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The positive value is genuinely representational because no uniform current-language action improves on the standing policy.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Acting on the row refinement, once acquired, means re-differentiating by row at the switching hurdle $\\kappa_i$; the post-refinement horizon gain remains exactly $\\tfrac12$, so the firm re-differentiates when $\\kappa_i<\\tfrac12$ and\u8212?knowing the row law yet finding the change not worth its cost\u8212?holds its old policy when $\\kappa_i\\geq\\tfrac12$, the deterministic face of enlightened inertia ([\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Under the model's two-stage timing it may still elect inquiry when the participation condition holds; in this transparent case, a hurdle at or above the exact gain makes later enlightened inertia foreseeable, a consequence of the deliberate timing convention rather than of unawareness.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The valuation used no conjecture about the rival and no reference to which refinement might arrive; transparency (winner-take-all) makes each $\\Theta_i(g)$ a singleton, so the deliberative estimate is exact.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For rational cessation and its converse, consider a later stretch that serves the two off-diagonal states, by which point firm 1 has acquired the row refinement (certain of the true assignment) while firm 2 has acquired the column refinement (certain of the false one): their policies differ at those states, firm 1 wins both, and the labels revealed there falsify firm 2's column theory.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For firm 1, both the fine and current-language values are zero, so $L_1^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}=L_1^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}=J_1=\\widehat B_1=0$: the firm holding the truth rationally never inquires again, and its awareness stays permanently incomplete.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For firm 2, two tokens disagree with its column policy and contribute $\\tfrac12$ each under fine contingency, while two agree and contribute zero, so $L_2^\{\\mathrm\{fine\}\}=1$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Within either current column, reversing the action gains $\\tfrac12$ on one token and loses $\\tfrac12$ on the other, so $L_2^\{\\mathrm\{cur\}\}=0$, $J_2=1$, and $\\widehat B_2=(2/4)1=\\tfrac12$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Defeat thus concentrates the evidence, dissonance, and incentive in the losing firm in this example, which elects whenever $\\lambda_2^\{(k_2)\}\\widehat B_2\\geq\\gamma_2$ and, upon success, reaches complete awareness in one step (both column cells must split).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The winner/loser asymmetry\u8212?$\\widehat B_1=0<\\widehat B_2$\u8212?is the durable point; the appendix records the exact value of $\\widehat B_2$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +## 9. The pivot: formulation, warrant, and the return to Bayes \{#sec-pivot\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Successful production yields a refinement $\\mathcal P_i'$; the truth-blind formulation rule selects $m'\\in\\widehat M_i^\{\\,R\}(\\mathcal P_i',\\bar r_i)$ from the repair-consistent theories on the recoded record; and the agent forms a full-support *bridge prior* $\\mu_i^\{+\}\\in\\Delta(M(\\mathcal P_i'))$, from which ordinary updating resumes.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Nothing in Bayesian coherence determines $\\mu_i^\{+\}$ from the pre-dissonance belief\u8212?the domains differ\u8212?and this nonuniqueness is not a defect to be repaired but the boundary between insight and judgment.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Write the complete realized post-insight output as $O_i=(\\mathcal P_i',m',\\mu_i^+)$, treating deterministic bridge-prior selection as a degenerate truth-blind selection rule.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Restricting and renormalizing $\\mu_i^\{+\}$ on $\\widehat M_i^\{\\,R\}(\\mathcal P_i',\\bar r_i)$ yields the initial acting belief on the refined language, whose probability assigned to the formulated theory is its *representation-relative coherence*:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\operatorname\{Coh\}_i(O_i)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\frac\{\\mu_i^+(m')\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\{\\displaystyle\\sum_\{\\widetilde m\\in\\widehat M_i^\{\\,R\}(\\mathcal P_i',\\bar r_i)\}\\mu_i^+(\\widetilde m)\}.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Formulation alone does not determine this probability: it depends jointly on the bridge prior and the repair-consistent active set, but is agent-computable once the refinement, recoded record, and bridge prior exist.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The question of this section is how much of that confidence the evidence actually licenses.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The conjecture on the refined partition is initialized from the recoded empirical frequencies of observed rival actions wherever the record contains observations, with a fixed default on previously unvisited cells, and is updated empirically thereafter.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Thus both inputs needed for the next standing policy\u8212?the bridge belief and the strategic conjecture\u8212?are defined on the expanded language only after the refinement has arrived.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Definition 9.1 (Reflective assessment, warrant, and signed gap) \{#def-warrant\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A reflective assessment problem is a pair $(\\mathcal T,\\nu)$: a finite set of candidate objective assignments and a full-support reflective prior.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +It is an *analyst-level* construct: conditioning on the events below uses the analyst record and the inquiry history.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Let $h_i$ denote the complete pre-production inquiry history, including prior elections, prior failures, prior successful production-and-formulation outputs, and the current partition generated by that history; in particular, the current pre-production partition $\\mathcal P_i$ is $h_i$-measurable.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +For a realized complete post-insight output $o=(\\mathcal P',m_o,\\mu^+)$, define its objective-correctness event by\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A_o\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\left\\\{\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\tau'\\in\\mathcal T:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\tau'(s)=m_o(C_\{\\mathcal P'\}(s))\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\text\{ for every \}s\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\right\\\}.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Its *selection-adjusted warrant*, relative to the specified assessment problem $(\\mathcal T,\\nu)$, is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +W(o)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\nu(A_o\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i,O_i=o).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The *signed warrant gap* at $o$ is $\\operatorname\{Coh\}_i(o)-W(o)$, whose sign is unrestricted in general.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Theorem 9.2 (No additional evidence beyond the generating record) \{#thm-uninformative\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Conditional on the analyst record $\\bar r_i$ and the pre-production inquiry history $h_i$, a record-measurable, truth-blind production, formulation, and bridge-prior-selection rule makes the complete output $O_i=(\\mathcal P_i',m',\\mu_i^+)$ conditionally independent of the candidate objective assignment.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Consequently, under the reflective joint law, for $K_i(\\,\\cdot\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i)$-almost every realized output $o$ and every $\\tau'\\in\\mathcal T$,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\nu(\\tau'\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i,O_i=o)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\nu(\\tau'\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +and therefore\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +W(o)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\nu(A_o\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Passing the repair test adds no information beyond the record because post-restoration fit is guaranteed by the successful-output construction.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +If candidates assign equal likelihood to $(\\bar r_i,h_i)$, their posterior odds remain their reflective prior odds.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  #### Proof \{#proof-thm-uninformative\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
