{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -blindness is the polar case; were production correlated with the objective\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -assignment\u8212?social transmission from an informed source\u8212?the arrival would\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -itself be evidence, and the adjustment could move confidence in either\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -direction.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -### Corollary 8.3 (Self-audit requires sufficiency for the candidates) \{#cor-self-audit\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -The assessment $(\\mathcal T,\\nu)$ is expressible by agent $i$ only if\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\mathcal P_i$ is sufficient for every $\\tau'\\in\\mathcal T$, hence only if\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\mathcal P_i$ refines the join of [proposition 6.6](#prop-robust-sufficiency).  An agent\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -holding a minimal restoration therefore generally cannot formulate the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -comparison that measures its own warrant gap: the overconfidence is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -invisible from within the representation that produces it.  Short of that\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -refinement, warrant must be supplied externally\u8212?by fresh evidence whose\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -likelihoods differ across candidates, by an assessor with broader awareness,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -or by a future self.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Let $Z_i=(\\bar r_i,h_i)$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Because $\\mathcal P_i$ is $h_i$-measurable and the complete output rule is record-measurable and truth-blind, its regular conditional output kernel $K_i(\\,\\cdot\\mid Z_i)$ is candidate-independent.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Thus, for every $\\tau'\\in\\mathcal T$ and every measurable output set $B$, the conditional joint law factors as\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\Pr(\\tau',O_i\\in B\\mid Z_i)\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +=\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\\nu(\\tau'\\mid Z_i)K_i(B\\mid Z_i).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +$$\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Election is determined by the deliberative record and failure history; production and formulation are truth-blind; and randomized bridge-prior selection is record-measurable and truth-blind.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The factorization establishes $O_i\\perp\\!\\!\\!\\perp\\tau'\\mid Z_i$ and hence the displayed posterior equality for $K_i(\\,\\cdot\\mid Z_i)$-almost every realized output $o$ and every candidate.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Summing that equality over the fixed event $A_o$ gives $W(o)=\\nu(A_o\\mid\\bar r_i,h_i)$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Passing the repair test is a deterministic implication of the record and realized output and therefore contributes no additional likelihood factor.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +If the record-and-history likelihoods are also equal across two candidates, their posterior odds equal their prior odds. \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In this precise conditional sense, the insight itself is not evidence: once the complete analyst record and inquiry history are held fixed, a truth-blind output adds no evidential content of its own.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +An agent or outside observer who does not possess the complete analyst record may genuinely learn from the output because it conveys information about the hidden particulars on which production operated.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The theorem prohibits treating that information as independent confirmation after the complete generating record has already entered the assessment; its practical force is a prohibition on double counting.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Truth blindness is the polar case; if production, formulation, or bridge-prior selection remains correlated with the objective assignment after conditioning on the record and history\u8212?as with transmission from an informed source\u8212?the output can supply a genuine Bayes factor, and the adjustment can move warrant in either direction.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Corollary 9.3 (Self-audit requires sufficiency for the candidates) \{#cor-self-audit\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The assessment $(\\mathcal T,\\nu)$ is expressible by agent $i$ only if its current post-refinement partition $\\mathcal P_i'$ is sufficient for every $\\tau'\\in\\mathcal T$, hence only if $\\mathcal P_i'$ refines the join of [proposition 7.5](#prop-robust-sufficiency).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +This is necessary but not sufficient for complete computation of warrant, which also requires a candidate set, a reflective prior, candidate likelihoods for the generating record and inquiry history, and the relevant selection rule.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +An agent holding a minimal restoration therefore generally cannot formulate the cross-representation comparison required to determine the sign or magnitude of its signed warrant gap.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A broader-awareness assessor may be able to formulate the comparison; fresh evidence changes reflective warrant only when its likelihood differs across the represented candidate worlds, and otherwise further awareness expansion may be required before the agent can use the evidence for that comparison.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  #### Proof \{#proof-cor-self-audit\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
