{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Performance differences persist not because an equilibrium concept freezes\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -them but because the process that would erase them has died economically:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the disadvantaged configuration generates no dissonance, or generates no\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -leverage, or prices its question below the cost of asking.  Terminal\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -heterogeneity in awareness is path dependence in the strong sense\u8212?agents\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -with identical preferences and identical Bayesian competence, facing the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -same objective system, end at different languages and different payoffs\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -because their histories posed different questions.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -### Definition 9.10 (Diagnostic environments) \{#def-diagnostic\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -The primitives $(\\Theta,\\tau,\\rho,u)$ are *diagnostic* if, under every\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -profile sustainable in a SCUE, every expressible theory that is\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -payoff-relevantly false\u8212?false at some state where the truth would change\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -its holder's optimal action\u8212?is $\\eta$-inadequate.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -### Proposition 9.11 (No payoff-relevant error in diagnostic environments) \{#prop-diagnostic\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -In a diagnostic environment, every SCUE is free of payoff-relevant error.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Payoff-relevant falsity survives only in environments that admit concealing\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -profiles, and it requires them to be sustained: collective error needs the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -absence of *both* corrective forces, strategic variety inside agents'\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -categories and environmental punishment of uniform misservice.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -#### Proof \{#proof-prop-diagnostic\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -By [definition 9.1](#def-scue)(iii), theories surviving in a SCUE are not\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -$\\eta$-inadequate; in a diagnostic environment every payoff-relevantly false\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -theory is.  The second claim restates [definition 5.4](#def-exposure): a false theory\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -survives only under concealing profiles, and [proposition 5.5](#prop-exposure) makes\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -concealment necessary as well as sufficient. \u8718?\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Suppose firm $i$'s technology produces the column refinement.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The recoded record pins the unique consistent theory: architecture $0$ on the first column, $1$ on the second.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Representation-relative coherence assigns it probability one.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Now conduct the reflective assessment with $\\mathcal T=\\\{\\text\{row world\},\\text\{column world\}\\\}$ and a symmetric prior.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The two worlds assign the realized diagonal-only record equal probability by the same coupling argument conditional on the diagonal-state event, and the technology is truth-blind, so by [theorem 9.2](#thm-uninformative) the reflective posterior equals the prior: $W(O_i)=\\tfrac12$, and the signed warrant gap is $1-\\tfrac12=+\\tfrac12$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The same example-specific gap applies to a firm that acquires the *row* refinement: its representation-relative coherence is also one, its warrant is also one-half, and confidence exceeds warrant even when the formulated theory happens to be objectively correct.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +By [corollary 9.3](#cor-self-audit), neither firm can conduct this assessment itself: expressing both candidate worlds requires the full partition into singletons.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +One fresh differentiated observation at an off-diagonal state resolves the row/column identification problem completely because the two worlds predict opposite labels there: if the formulated theory is correct, $W(O_i)$ rises to one and the positive signed gap closes; if it is false, it is rejected, the singleton active set empties, and the acting belief becomes undefined.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At $\\beta=1$ under pooled play, any number of pooled observations remains nondiagnostic between the row and column worlds.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In this four-state laboratory at $\\beta=1$, differentiated play purchases the evidence that separates the row and column worlds; pooled play does not.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +## 10. Strategic dynamics: when everyone lives in a Bayesian world \{#sec-dynamics\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The chain now runs inside a population.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Theories determine standing policies; policies determine which conditionals are visited; visited conditionals determine dissonance and leverage; and refinements feed back into theories.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +This section characterizes where the process comes to rest.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The object of interest is not a strategic equilibrium but an epistemic condition: a configuration of the population in which *every agent permanently inhabits a Bayesian world*\u8212?models fit, questions are dead, and no represented calculation prices further inquiry above its cost.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Definition 10.1 (Self-confirming unawareness equilibrium) \{#def-scue\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A profile of epistemic states $\\xi_i=(\\mathcal P_i,r_i,\\bar\\mu_i,q_i,\\sigma_i,k_i)$, $i\\in N$\u8212?awareness, retained record, reference posterior, conjecture, standing policy, and failure counter, with acting beliefs $\\mu_i$ derived by judged updating\u8212?is a *self-confirming unawareness equilibrium* (SCUE) if, under the play it induces,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (i) each standing policy is stationary under the switching rule of [assumption 4.4](#ass-commitment): no switch clears the hurdle, $T\\,[\\,U_i(\\sigma_i^\{\\star\}\\mid\\mu_i,q_i)-U_i(\\sigma_i\\mid\\mu_i,q_i)\\,]\\le\\kappa_i$, which is subjective optimality itself when $\\kappa_i=0$;\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (ii) each conjecture $q_i$ agrees, in the limit of its empirical frequencies, with the play induced by $\\sigma_\{-i\}$ at every on-path cell;\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (iii) no dissonance survives: each agent's active set, computed from its record as play accumulates, is almost surely eventually nonempty, and the acting-belief mass on any $\\eta$-inadequate theory vanishes almost surely; and\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (iv) no agent elects inquiry: $\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i(r_i)<\\gamma_i$ along the induced records, which holds in particular whenever $\\widehat B_i=0$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The record and failure counter belong in the state: dissonance status, leverage, and the achievability weight are functions of retained evidence and inquiry history, so two histories with identical partitions, beliefs, and policies but different records can differ in equilibrium status.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Conditions (ii)\u8211?(iii) are stated asymptotically because empirical conjectures and stochastic tests fluctuate at finite samples.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Deterministic consequence mechanisms make a contradictory test observation irreversible, but they do not eliminate sampling variation in states or in rivals' actions within an agent's awareness cell; empirical conjectures therefore generally still converge only asymptotically.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Conditions (i)\u8211?(ii) are subjective rationality with confirmed conjectures: the self-confirming conditions of the fixed-language tradition (Fudenberg and Levine 1993; Kalai and Lehrer 1993).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Conditions (iii)\u8211?(iv) are the new, epistemic ones: the language survives its own evidence, and the question has no priced value.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A SCUE in which every partition is sufficient for $\\tau$ and beliefs concentrate near the truth is simply a self-confirming equilibrium; the concept's interest lies entirely in the other cases.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Definition 10.2 (Dissonant stasis) \{#def-stasis\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Agent $i$ is in *dissonant stasis* from some period on if dissonance recurs while it never both elects and succeeds\u8212?because $\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i(r_i)<\\gamma_i$ (no priced repair: zero leverage, or an abandoned question after the achievability weight has decayed, possibly at an irreparable record), or because elected production fails at every subsequent attempt.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Its standing policy is carried forward with a standing anomaly.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A population profile is *absorbing* if every agent is, from some period on, either in a SCUE role (never dissonant) or in dissonant stasis.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Table 2 collects the taxonomy of terminal conditions developed in this section, including the enlightened inertia of [\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +**Table 2.** Taxonomy of terminal conditions: how questions die.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +| Terminal condition | What survives | Why inquiry died | Payoff consequence | Example instance |\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +|---|---|---|---|---|\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +| SCUE ([definition 10.1](#def-scue)) | a represented model class adequate on path, with acting beliefs on it | answered, or never priced: $\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i<\\gamma_i$, in particular $\\widehat B_i=0$ | can be first-best, or carry concealed payoff-relevant error | the $\\beta=1$ trap: both firms certain of the false column law, each earning $\\tfrac12$ forever |\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +| Dissonant stasis ([definition 10.2](#def-stasis)) | no admitted theory; the standing policy carries a standing anomaly | unpriced ($\\widehat B_i=0$), abandoned ($\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$ decayed), or unanswerable (irreparable record) | permanent disadvantage possible | at $\\beta<1$: the coarse firm earns $\\tfrac14$ against its refined rival's $\\tfrac34$, permanently |\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +| Enlightened inertia ([\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness)) | a refined language and an improved model, learned but not acted on | answered, but the recommended switch is unpriced: horizon-$T$ gain $\\le\\kappa_i$ | the agent forgoes the improvement its rival captures | $\\kappa_i\\ge\\tfrac12$ after acquiring the row law: the firm knows it and holds its old policy |\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### A represented model class, restored endogenously \{#rem-grain\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Rational-learning convergence traditionally requires a grain of truth: the environment is absolutely continuous with respect to beliefs (Kalai and Lehrer 1993).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Under unawareness the objective assignment may be inexpressible on the current language.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Causal dissonance is the model's operational signal that no admitted theory survives the current evidence; in the stochastic setting it is not by itself proof that the objective truth is inexpressible.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Successful refinement restores a nonempty represented model class consistent with the retained record.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +It does not by itself establish objective correctness or future on-path adequacy; subsequent experience determines whether the restored language survives.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +A SCUE is a configuration in which an admitted represented model class continues to survive on path and no agent has a priced reason to seek a finer one.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Assumption 10.3 (Regularity) \{#ass-regularity\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +(i) *Strict adequacy.*\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At each visited pair every theory is either $\\eta$-adequate or strictly inadequate\u8212?none sits exactly at the adequacy boundary\u8212?so [lemma D.1](../appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency) applies for every agent, theory, partition profile, and policy profile.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +(ii) *Production randomness.*\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The randomization in each $\\phi_i$ is independent across elections and of the state and consequence draws, and, conditional on an election at a *repairable* record ($\\mathcal R(\\mathcal P_i,\\bar r_i)\\neq\\emptysetset$), production succeeds with probability at least $\\underline\\pi>0$.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At an irreparable record production fails surely ([definition 7.2](#def-technology)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Part (i) is the genericity that makes each theory's evidence process settle cleanly relative to the capacity threshold ([lemma D.1](../appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency)); it rules out only a boundary knife-edge and holds automatically under the exact calibration ([\u8220?The Calibration Convention\u8221?](#conv-calibration)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Part (ii) gives every elected repairable question a real chance of resolution; finiteness of elections comes instead from the decay of the achievability weight, so no separate never-produce exclusion is needed.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The agent, unable to tell a repairable record from an irreparable one, may elect either; the two are distinguished only in their success probabilities, not in the agent's decision.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Theorem 10.4 (Epistemic absorption) \{#thm-absorption\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Under [assumption 10.3](#ass-regularity), almost surely:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (a) at most $n(|S|-1)$ refinements occur, and every agent's awareness partition is eventually constant;\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (b) only finitely many inquiry elections occur\u8212?each agent stops electing once its achievability weight has decayed enough that $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}\\,T(\\max \\pi_i-\\min \\pi_i)<\\gamma_i$, and this happens after finitely many consecutive failures because $\\widehat B_i$ is bounded and $\\gamma_i>0$; and\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (c) there is an almost surely finite period after which no agent's language changes and no agent pays an inquiry cost: every agent's epistemic life thereafter is judged-Bayesian updating within a fixed language, punctuated at most by belief-driven policy switches under [assumption 4.4](#ass-commitment) and by dissonance events that fail the participation threshold.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Moreover, on the event that the standing profile is eventually constant,\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +- (d) every agent's active set is eventually constant; every theory retained in that eventual active set is $\\eta$-adequate at every recurrent pair under terminal play, every theory $\\eta$-inadequate at a recurrent pair under terminal play is eventually absent, and each agent is eventually either never dissonant\u8212?it lives in a Bayesian world\u8212?or in dissonant stasis ([definition 10.2](#def-stasis)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The proof is in [appendix B](../appendix/appendix.md#app-absorption).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Converging non-stasis configurations limit to a partial SCUE, and a SCUE configuration with strict optimality margins and zero leverage persists\u8212?exactly with deterministic mechanisms, and with probability at least $1-\\sum_i e^\{-b_i\}$ in the stochastic case, so capacity governs the robustness of a rest point; the formal statement is [proposition D.5](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-rest-points) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred), with proof in [appendix B](../appendix/appendix.md#app-absorption).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### What the theorem does and does not claim \{#rem-scope\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +[Theorem 10.4](#thm-absorption) is a statement about the epistemic process\u8212?the death of inquiry\u8212?not about the convergence of play.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Within a Bayesian world, standing policies may in principle continue to cycle as beliefs and conjectures chase one another; that is the classical convergence problem of learning in games (Fudenberg and Levine 1993; Kalai and Lehrer 1993), it is orthogonal to this paper's contribution, and the theorem deliberately does not resolve it.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Part (d) and the rest-point characterization are accordingly conditional on play stabilizing, which in every configuration featured in this paper is immediate: their beliefs make one action per cell strictly dominant.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Switching costs temper the cycling: the inaction band absorbs belief fluctuations too small to be worth acting on, so only swings whose horizon-$T$ gain exceeds $\\kappa_i$ move play\u8212?a stabilizing force, though not one that rules out large-amplitude cycles.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The decay of $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$ is what makes inquiry die out even when the question is genuine: an agent facing a true, valuable, but hard-to-repair defect abandons it once repeated failure has eroded its hope.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Abandoned questions are thus a substantive absorbing outcome, not an artifact\u8212?inquiry ceases because it is answered, because it is unpriced, or because it is given up.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Were $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}$ held fixed instead of decaying, an agent could elect a doomed inquiry forever, paying $\\gamma_i$ each period for a repair that never arrives; the decay rules this out and is the model's account of when a rational inquirer stops.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Rational anomaly tolerance \{#rem-anomaly\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Zero-leverage dissonant stasis is a recognizable condition, not a pathology of the model: the agent registers that no admitted theory survives its test\u8212?yet its deliberative valuation finds no coherent grouping with positive representational increment, so repairing the account is worth nothing to it.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Standing anomalies tolerated by working scientists and managers have exactly this structure, and the model locates them: anomaly tolerance is rational precisely when the agent's coherent groupings carry no gross representational leverage.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Two sharper instances complete the taxonomy.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +At an irreparable record ([remark D.3](../appendix/appendix.md#rem-irreparable)) no expressible repair exists at any price\u8212?the anomaly is not merely unprofitable but impossible to fix within the current grammar\u8212?though the agent, unable to certify irreparability under noise, may keep electing while its deliberative record supports positive leverage and until the achievability weight decays.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +And an *abandoned question* is a repairable, positively-valued defect the agent stops pursuing because repeated failure has driven $\\lambda_i^\{(k)\}\\widehat B_i$ below cost: rational surrender, not indifference.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In a SCUE, surviving error lives only in what play never exposes: acting-belief mass on every $\\eta$-inadequate theory vanishes, and all retained falsity is confined to pooled mechanism assignments within tolerance at visited profiles and to counterfactual claims at unvisited profiles ([proposition D.6](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-adequacy), [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In stochastic environments capacity is a single cognitive-style dial\u8212?expected detection time under an exposed profile is $O(b_i/D_i)$ while spurious dissonance at a non-exposed rest point has probability at most $e^\{-b_i\}$\u8212?and it plays no role in the exact deterministic case; the formal statement and proof are [proposition D.7](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-capacity) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Proposition 10.5 (Persistent performance differences) \{#prop-persistence\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +There exist primitives and absorbing configurations in which agents hold different terminal partitions and theories, and expected per-period payoffs differ strictly and permanently, with no disadvantaged agent closing the gap\u8212?because for each the corrective process has died economically at one of its two stages: either its question is unpriced (*dissonant stasis*, $\\lambda_i^\{(k_i)\}\\widehat B_i(r_i)<\\gamma_i$ from some period on), or, having asked and refined, the policy change its new model recommends is priced below the switching hurdle (*enlightened inertia*, $T$-horizon gain $\\le\\kappa_i$, [\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The stasis channel is established by the instance below; the enlightened-inertia channel is the deterministic possibility of [\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness) (a firm that acquires the true distinction yet, facing $\\kappa_i$ above the gain, forgoes the improvement its rival captures). The mechanism deserves emphasis.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Performance differences persist not because an equilibrium concept freezes them but because the process that would erase them has died economically: the disadvantaged agent's question is priced below the cost of asking\u8212?through zero leverage, an eroded achievability weight, or an irreparable record\u8212?or, having asked and learned, it finds the switch its new model recommends priced below the hurdle and holds its old policy ([\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness)).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Terminal heterogeneity in awareness is path dependence in the strong sense\u8212?agents with identical preferences and identical Bayesian competence, facing the same objective system, end at different languages and different payoffs because their histories posed different questions.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Two sources of heterogeneity \{#rem-two-sources\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Terminal heterogeneity has two independent origins here.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Agents identical in preferences, competence, capacity, and cost can still end at different languages and payoffs, because their histories posed different questions and their truth-blind technologies produced different repairs\u8212?path dependence that begins before probability.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Agents identical in *everything* but their dissonance capacity $b_i$ and switching hurdle $\\kappa_i$ also diverge: in stochastic environments capacity affects detection speed and the robustness of rest points ([proposition D.7](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-capacity)), while the hurdle sets the propensity to enlightened inertia ([\u8220?Enlightened inertia\u8221?](#rem-stickiness)); the capacity channel disappears under exact deterministic contradiction.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The first is the awareness-path microfoundation; the second a parametric cognitive-style one\u8212?and neither is available in the fixed-language tradition.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In environments whose primitives are *diagnostic*\u8212?payoff-relevant policy errors always expose the erring agent's awareness under confirmed stationary play\u8212?no SCUE contains a payoff-relevant policy error; the formal apparatus is [definition D.8](../appendix/appendix.md#def-diagnostic) and [proposition D.9](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-diagnostic) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +### Concealment is necessary, not sufficient \{#concealment-is-necessary-not-sufficient\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +By [proposition D.6](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-adequacy), an objectively false theory that retains nonvanishing acting-belief mass in a stable SCUE must be $\\eta$-adequate on path; the induced profile is therefore concealing for that theory in the sense of [definition 6.4](#def-exposure).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Concealment alone does not guarantee survival.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +The theory must also be admitted when the language is initialized, avoid prior and subsequent rejection, retain nonvanishing acting-belief mass, support a stationary standing policy, coexist with confirmed conjectures, and leave no profitable inquiry election.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +In stochastic environments even an active $\\eta$-adequate theory remains subject to the conditional false-rejection bound of [lemma D.1](../appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency); under the exact calibration false rejection is impossible ([\u8220?The Calibration Convention\u8221?](#conv-calibration)), but the remaining SCUE conditions are still required.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Strictly punishing primitives\u8212?those whose on-path conditionals at every payoff-relevant policy error separate from every expressible prediction by more than $\\eta$\u8212?are diagnostic, as [proposition D.10](../appendix/appendix.md#prop-punishing) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred) records.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +Strict payoff and separation margins at a fixed profile survive small perturbations of the primitives, though this is a local stability property rather than openness of global diagnosticity; see [remark D.11](../appendix/appendix.md#rem-local-robustness) in [appendix D](../appendix/appendix.md#app-deferred).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  ### Example 1 (continued) \{#example-1-continued-6\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Set $\\beta=1$ and suppose both firms acquired the column refinement after\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -the discovery generation and became certain of the false column assignment.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -Each then plays the column policy; the firms pool at every state; every\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -payoff is one-half; and one-half is exactly what the column theory predicts\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -under pooled play.  The configuration is a SCUE with payoff-relevant error:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -policies are subjectively optimal, conjectures confirmed, no dissonance ever\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -occurs (the profile is concealing), and $B_i=0$ for both firms\u8212?so the\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -configuration survives even a free, infallible inquiry technology.  The\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -warrant gap of [section 8](#sec-pivot) is permanent: unbounded experience\par}
