{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - "for the second claim: no single theory is eta-adequate under both worlds at the visited pairs"\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: The rule's input is the record, whose distribution is identical by hypothesis, so its output distribution is identical in the two worlds.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - common initial epistemic states\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - record-measurable behavioral and tie-breaking rules\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - truth-blind inquiry-and-formulation rules\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - consequence laws agree at every\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Couple the two worlds on common state draws, common independent seeds for production, formulation, bridge-prior selection and tie-breaking, and identical joint consequence draws at every reachable pair.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [appendix/appendix.md#probability-framework]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: "Induction over periods: identical histories give identical partitions and standing policies, hence the same action profile at the common state; the pair is reachable, so both assignments give it the same joint consequence distribution and the coupled consequence profiles coincide; both records stay identical."\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#ass-observation, paper/paper.md#ass-commitment]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Record-measurability and truth-blindness give identical belief updates, conjectures, policies, refinements and formulations, closing the induction through H; the all-horizons claim follows by countability.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-technology, paper/paper.md#def-formulation-rule]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Every truth-blind rule therefore has the same output distribution in the two worlds; since tau differs from tau', their sets of objectively correct formulations are disjoint, and one distribution cannot assign probability one to both; the same holds for any disjoint pair of success sets.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0          uses: [paper/paper.md#def-technology]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: If the adequate sets are disjoint, any realized output is inadequate in at least one world with the corresponding probability, so no truth-blind rule selects an adequate formulation with probability one in both.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-test]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    conclusion: Any truth-blind technology or inquiry-and-formulation rule has the same output distribution in both worlds, and when no theory is eta-adequate in both, none selects an adequate formulation with probability one in both.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: The two worlds admit a pathwise coupling through H, and no truth-blind rule is correct with probability one in both.\par}
