{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0    - id: D12\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      states: paper/paper.md#thm-uninformative\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    hypotheses:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - the technology is truth-blind\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - "a reflective assessment problem (T, nu): a finite candidate set and a full-support reflective prior"\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: The reflective posterior on tau' in T is proportional to nu(tau'), times the record's likelihood under tau', times the probability of the production event given the record.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-warrant, "cited: Bayes' rule"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: Truth blindness makes the last factor a function of the record alone, constant across T, so it cancels and W equals the ordinary reflective posterior of m''s correctness given the record alone.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-technology, paper/paper.md#def-warrant]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: Fit is a deterministic function of record and output, hence has likelihood one in every world consistent with the event, so passing the test carries no information beyond the record either.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: ["truth-blind production, formulation, and bridge-prior-selection rule"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Let Z_i be the analyst record and the inquiry history; P_i is h_i-measurable and the complete output rule is record-measurable and truth-blind, so its regular conditional output kernel K_i(.|Z_i) is candidate-independent.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-warrant, paper/paper.md#def-technology, paper/paper.md#def-formulation-rule]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: The conditional joint law factors as nu(tau'|Z_i) K_i(B|Z_i), since election is determined by the deliberative record and failure history, production and formulation are truth-blind, and randomized bridge-prior selection is record-measurable and truth-blind.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#ass-elective, paper/paper.md#def-technology]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: The factorization gives O_i independent of tau' given Z_i, hence the posterior equality for K_i-almost every output; summing over the fixed event A_o gives W(o) = nu(A_o | record, history).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-warrant]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Passing the repair test is a deterministic implication of the record and the realized output and so contributes no likelihood factor; equal record-and-history likelihoods leave posterior odds at prior odds.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0          uses: [paper/paper.md#def-restorative]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -      - says: Applying the cancellation to candidates with identical record likelihoods preserves their prior odds exactly.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-warrant]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    conclusion: Conditioning on the production event adds nothing to the record; W equals the reflective posterior given the record alone; passing the test is uninformative; and among candidates inducing the same record distribution, prior odds are preserved exactly.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: Conditional on the analyst record and the inquiry history, the complete output is independent of the candidate objective assignment, and warrant equals the reflective probability of correctness given record and history alone.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0  \par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0    - id: D13\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      states: paper/paper.md#cor-self-audit\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    hypotheses: ["the assessment (T, nu) is expressible by agent i"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: ["the assessment"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0        - says: Entertaining tau' as a hypothesis requires expressing it, which is sufficiency for tau'.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0          uses: [paper/paper.md#def-awareness, paper/paper.md#def-warrant]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0        - says: Sufficiency for every candidate is refinement of the join.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0          uses: [paper/paper.md#prop-robust-sufficiency]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 -    conclusion: The assessment is expressible by agent i only if P_i is sufficient for every candidate, hence only if P_i refines the join of the candidates' causal-equivalence partitions.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: The assessment is expressible by the agent only if its post-refinement partition refines the join of the candidates' partitions.\par}
