{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0    - id: D14\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      states: paper/paper.md#thm-absorption\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0      symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: ["Assumption 10.3"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: (a) Each successful production strictly refines one agent's partition and no partition ever coarsens; the total cell count is an integer that starts at no less than n, never exceeds n|S| and rises at every success, so at most n(|S| - 1) successes occur and every partition is eventually constant.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#ass-elective, appendix/appendix.md#part-a, derivations:D5]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: (b) B_i <= T Delta pi_i; if Delta pi_i = 0 no election occurs since gamma_i > 0; otherwise the election condition fails once lambda^(k) < gamma_i / (T Delta pi_i), which happens at a finite failure count because lambda^(k) is nonincreasing to 0; the counter resets only on a success, of which there are finitely many, so elections are finite on every path.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#prop-participation, paper/paper.md#ass-elective, appendix/appendix.md#part-b]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: (c) After the later of the last refinement and the last election, no language changes and no inquiry cost is paid; every later dissonance event fails the participation threshold; all other activity is judged-Bayesian updating in a fixed language.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#judged-updating, appendix/appendix.md#part-c]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: (d) On the event that the standing profile is eventually constant, decompose it by (period, profile) and couple the process to an auxiliary one that plays the constant profile; recurrent pairs are visited with fixed positive probability, so empirical conditionals converge by the strong law; under Assumption 10.3(i) the test-consistency lemma makes each active set eventually a survivor set of eta-adequate theories; a nonempty survivor set means the agent is eventually never dissonant, an empty one means dissonant stasis, since no election occurs after G*.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [appendix/appendix.md#probability-framework, appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency, paper/paper.md#ass-regularity, paper/paper.md#def-stasis, appendix/appendix.md#part-d]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: Almost surely refinements and elections are finite and every agent's language and inquiry costs stop; on the eventually-constant-profile event each agent is eventually never dissonant or in dissonant stasis.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +  - id: D15\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    states: paper/paper.md#prop-persistence\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: []\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: "Stasis channel, by instance: take beta < 1, firm 1 on the row law and firm 2 constant on one architecture; expected payoffs are 3/4 and 1/4 under uniform rho; firm 2's record rejects all three constant theories, so it is dissonant; its leverage is 1/2 on the balanced four-token record and positive and bounded in general; permanent stasis holds when gamma_2 exceeds lambda_2^(k) B_2 along the continuation, for which gamma_2 > lambda_2^(k) T Delta pi_2 suffices."\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [appendix/appendix.md#persistence-payoffs, paper/paper.md#def-stasis, paper/paper.md#prop-participation, derivations:D6, derivations:D2]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: "Enlightened-inertia channel: a firm that acquires the row law faces a post-refinement horizon gain of exactly 1/2 and holds its old policy when kappa_i >= 1/2."\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#rem-stickiness, paper/paper.md#ass-commitment]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: The configuration is absorbing, so the difference is permanent.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#thm-absorption, appendix/appendix.md#prop-rest-points]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: There exist primitives and absorbing configurations with different terminal languages and strictly, permanently different payoffs, the corrective process having died at one of its two stages.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +  - id: D16\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    states: appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: ["either eta-adequate or strictly inadequate at each visited pair"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: A recurrent pair is visited each period with fixed positive probability under the i.i.d. full-support draw, hence infinitely often; a frozen pair only in the finite prefix, affecting only the inherited value E_i^m(t_0).\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#ass-observation, appendix/appendix.md#probability-framework]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: For a theory strictly inadequate at a recurrent pair, the construction supplies a fixed betting component with strictly positive expected log-growth and positive weight; component domination and the strong law make the evidence process diverge, so log E crosses b_i and the theory is rejected.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [appendix/appendix.md#app-eprocess, paper/paper.md#def-test]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: For a theory adequate at every recurrent post-t_0 pair, the evidence process is a nonnegative supermartingale and conditional Ville's inequality bounds the future rejection probability by E_i^m(t_0) e^\{-b_i\}.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [appendix/appendix.md#app-eprocess, derivations:D4]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: No re-entry, permanence of rejection and finiteness of M(P_i) make the active set monotone and eventually constant; collecting the two cases gives the dissonance dichotomy.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-test, paper/paper.md#def-dissonance]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: Inadequate active theories are eventually rejected, adequate ones survive with the stated conditional probability, and eventual dissonance is almost sure exactly when every expressible theory falls under the first case.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +\par}
