{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: M(P') is the set of cell-constant assignments Theta^\{P'\}, and every constraint of the repair test involves only the mechanism assigned to one cell, so the repair-consistent set is the product over cells of the cellwise consistent sets.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-awareness, paper/paper.md#def-restorative]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: A product of finite sets is nonempty exactly when every factor is nonempty.\par}
