{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    kind: proof\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    states: appendix/appendix.md#prop-diagnostic\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    symbols: \{\}\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    hypotheses: ["diagnostic at tolerance"]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    steps:\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Suppose a SCUE contains a payoff-relevant policy error for agent i; every SCUE satisfies conditions (i)-(ii), so diagnosticity makes P_i exposed under the induced standing profile.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-scue, appendix/appendix.md#def-diagnostic]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: Exposure means every theory active on that language is eta-inadequate at some recurrent on-path pair; by the test-consistency lemma each is eventually rejected and none re-enters; finiteness of M(P_i) empties the active set almost surely.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-exposure, appendix/appendix.md#lem-test-consistency]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +      - says: That contradicts SCUE condition (iii), which requires the active set to be almost surely eventually nonempty.\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +        uses: [paper/paper.md#def-scue]\par}
{\pard\f1\fs20\sa0 +    conclusion: In a diagnostic environment no SCUE contains a payoff-relevant policy error.\par}
